{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid5790295 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  Acknowledgments}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Acknowledgments}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Acknowledgments}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Acknowledgments
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 Eudora WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is based on the Freeware IMS for Windows NT that was developed under the EMWAC project.  EMWAC was funded by Datalink Computers, Digital, Microsoft, Research Machines, Sequent and the University of Edinburgh.
\par Certain algorithms used in parts of this software are derived from the RSA Data Security, Inc. MD5 Message-Digest Algorithm.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid5790295 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  Introduction}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Introduction}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Introduction}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Introduction
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Welcome to }{\insrsid3152417 Eudora WorldMail}{\super\insrsid4720447 \'99}{\insrsid7218531 , from }{\insrsid3152417 QUALCOMM}{\insrsid7218531 , Inc}{\insrsid3152417 orporated}{\insrsid7218531 .}{\super\insrsid7218531 \'ae}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is an Internet Mail and List Server for Microsoft Windows platforms. }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  allows your computer to host e-mail accounts and mail lists, and to communicate with other Internet mail servers to send and receive e-mail. }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is 100% compliant with Internet electronic mail standards, including the SMTP, POP3, IMAP4, and LDAP3 RFC specifications.
\par }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's main job is to host }{\i\insrsid7218531 mailboxes}{\insrsid7218531 , which correspond to individual e-mail users. Each }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox can be configured to forward mail to another address, and to automatically respond to incoming mail with a pre-defined message. You can create one or more }{\i\insrsid7218531 aliases}{\insrsid7218531  for each mailbox, allowing a single user to receive e-mail sent to multiple addresses. Users can access e-mail in their }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailboxes with any POP3 or IMAP4 mail client, such as }{\insrsid13446336 Eudora}{\insrsid7218531 , and can also use a web browser to check their mail through the }{\insrsid16389365 Eudora Web Client}{\insrsid7218531  webmail application. Users can even manage their own mailboxes through a standard web browser.
\par You can also create }{\i\insrsid7218531 mail lists}{\insrsid7218531  on your }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  server. Mail lists allow messages sent to a single e-mail address to be broadcast to any number of }{\i\insrsid7218531 members}{\insrsid7218531 . You can control the access and security of each list, and delegate mail list administrative duties.
\par }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  includes extensive }{\i\insrsid7218531 spam blocking}{\insrsid7218531 , }{\i\insrsid7218531 virus detection}{\insrsid7218531 , and other SMTP security features. }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can automatically protect your site from destructive or offensive emails, denial-of-service attacks, and third-party relaying.
\par }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  provides powerful mail }{\i\insrsid7218531 routing}{\insrsid7218531  capabilities. It can act as a staging post for mail destined for another host, which is useful for creating an e-mail proxy or relay server.
\par }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports }{\i\insrsid7218531 virtual domains}{\insrsid7218531 , so you can configure a single }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  server to send and receive mail for multiple domains. 
\par }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  also supports }{\i\insrsid7218531 dialup networking}{\insrsid7218531 , allowing your }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  server to connect to your ISP or central office to send and receive mail intermittently.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid5790295 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailSitePackagingOptions}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  WorldMail Packaging Options}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  WorldMail Packaging Options}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Packaging Options
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid9122794 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid3152417\charrsid9122794 Eudora WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531\charrsid9122794  
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid3152417 Eudora WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is a full-featured mail server that is easy to install and maintain.  It has been designed with the nonprofessional administrator in mind. It does not require extensive training or advanced certification in order to install and operate. This means that smaller companies don't need to employ a full time administrator to run their email system. }{\insrsid3152417 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is also an attractive choice for service providers who offer dedicated hosted email services.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Spam Filter
\par }\pard\plain \s114\ql \tx360\li360\ri130\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx1440\tx2160\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn360\lin360\itap0\pararsid11432085 \f4\fs16\lang2057\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Spam Filter is a part of the new }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid15275290 3}{\insrsid7218531  product line introduction. It is a next-generation spam blocking solution that uses a "cocktail" approach of technologies to detect and eliminate spam. By providing end-user controls, false positives are avoided. }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Spam Filter analyzes email during processing, to identify spam before it's delivered. Configuration options allow end users to review their server-identified spam, or an automated server quarantine of spam can be used.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Virus Filter
\par }\pard\plain \s114\ql \tx360\li360\ri130\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx1440\tx2160\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn360\lin360\itap0\pararsid11432085 \f4\fs16\lang2057\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Virus Filter is an integrated }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  add-in that blocks viruses at their network entry point - the email server. This prevents them from getting past user defenses and protects corporate data. }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Virus Filter detects and removes viruses, worms and Trojans from incoming, outgoing and internal email traffic in real time, before viruses can enter or leave the network.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid5790295 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailSiteComponents}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  WorldMail Components}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  WorldMail Components}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Components
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Components}}}{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is comprised of two basic components: the }{\i\insrsid7218531 Engine}{\insrsid7218531 , which provides e-mail-related services, and }{\i\insrsid14683656 Management Centers}{\insrsid7218531 , which provide administrative access to configuration values and mailbox data.  If your license supports it, }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  also provides access to mailboxes through the }{\insrsid16389365 Eudora Web Client}{\insrsid7218531  webmail interface.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Engine }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Engine}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 At the heart of }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is the Engine, a series of services that allow }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to send, receive, and deliver e-mail messages. The Engine also includes services that provide access to mailbox and mail list configuration information, and others that allow end users to retrieve their mail. The Engine's services typically run continuously on your server machine, and are equivalent to UNIX daemons such as sendmail and pop3.
\par The Engine includes the following services, which can be started and stopped independent of each other:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls135\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls135\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\insrsid7218531 SMTP Receiver Service}{\insrsid7218531 . The Receiver Service listens for incoming messages from other mail servers on the Internet.  It stores incoming messages for processing by the Delivery Service.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls135\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls135\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\insrsid7218531 SMTP Delivery Service}{\insrsid7218531 . The Delivery Service is the core of the Engine. It delivers mail addressed to local users to their mailboxes and forwards other mail out onto the Internet. It uses MX records from your DNS server for routing mail.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls135\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls135\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\insrsid7218531 POP3 Service}{\insrsid7218531 . The POP Service allows users to download mail from their mailboxes to their own computer using a POP3 mail client, such as }{\insrsid13446336 Eudora}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls135\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls135\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\insrsid7218531 IMAP4 Service}{\insrsid7218531 . The IMAP Service allows users to read mail in their mailboxes using an IMAP4 mail client.  IMAP users can also create folders within their mailboxes to organize messages.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls135\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls135\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\insrsid7218531 LDAP3 Directory Service}{\insrsid7218531 . The LDAP Directory Service allows users to search for names and addresses of other users who have mailboxes on your site.  It is fully compatible with e-mail clients that support the LDAP3 protocol for address searches.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls135\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls135\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\insrsid7218531 HTTP Management Agent}{\insrsid7218531 . The HTTP Management Agent allows administrators and users to remotely manage mailboxes and mail lists using a web browser.  It is fully compatible with web browsers that support the HTML 2.0 and later standards, such as Microsoft Internet Explorer and Netscape Navigator.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls135\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls135\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\insrsid7218531 Mail Management Service}{\insrsid7218531 . The Mail Management Service allows you to remotely manage the mail server using the Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .  It also allows users of the Eudora mail client to change their password from Eudora.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Windows Management }{\insrsid14683656 Center}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Management Centers,Windows}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Windows Management Center}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The Windows Management }{\insrsid14683656 Center}{\insrsid7218531  is a Windows desktop application that allows you to configure all aspects of }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , including the Engine services, domains, mailboxes, and mail lists.  Among the operations that you can perform in the Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  are starting and stopping services, setting security policies, setting delivery schedules, creating and modifying mailboxes, and creating and modifying mail lists.  Although the Web }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  provides access to managing mailboxes and mail lists, the Engine can be managed only from Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par The Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  can be installed on a different computer than the one that runs the }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Engine. This means that you can run the Engine on a large server system but still manage it from your desktop computer using the Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .  The Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  can manage multiple instances of }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , so if you have }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  installed on two or more server machines, you can manage all of them from one Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Web Management }{\insrsid14683656 Center}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Management Centers,Web}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Web Management Center}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The Web Management }{\insrsid14683656 Center}{\insrsid7218531  provides access to }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailboxes and mail lists through a web browser, and can be used remotely.  The Web }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  supports Internet Explorer 2.0 (and above), Netscape Navigator 2.0 (and above), and any other browser that supports HTML 2.0 and later.  This interface is typically used by domain administrators, mail list moderators, and end users.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid16389365 Eudora Web Client}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Eudora Web Client}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid16389365 Eudora Web Client}{\insrsid7218531  is a full-featured web-based mail client that allows users to access their mailboxes through a web browser from any computer on the Internet.  This allows your users to send and receive e-mail even if they are away from their own computers.  Users can also organize their messages into folders and maintain an address book.  }{\insrsid16389365 Eudora Web Client}{\insrsid7218531  is implemented using HTML and JavaScript, and does not require any complex installation of Java or ActiveX controls.  }{\insrsid16389365 Eudora Web Client}{\insrsid7218531  is compatible with Internet Explorer 4.0 (and above) and Netscape Navigator 4.0 (and above).
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid5533515 Eudora Connect}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Eudora Connect}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid5533515 Eudora Connect}{\insrsid7218531  is an email client for Wireless Access Protocol (WAP) devices. }{\insrsid5533515 Eudora Connect}{\insrsid7218531  allows users to access their mailboxes through any WAP-compatible device, such as cellular phones and other wireless Internet devices. Users can read messages, move messages between folders, and delete messages.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  KeyMailSiteFeatures}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Key WorldMail Features}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Key WorldMail Features}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  Key }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Features
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Features}}}{\insrsid7218531 This section provides an overview of some of }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's many features.  If you are upgrading from a previous version of }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  and want to know which features are new to this version, see the following section.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Extremely Scalable
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can support an extremely large number of users, scaling to over 100,000 mailboxes on a single Windows 2000 server or on a cluster of servers.  }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can also support over 100,000 members in a single mail list. Administrators can configure all }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  servers in a cluster to be clones or to have specified roles (e.g. just inbound SMTP, just IMAP, etc.)
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 High Performance Engine
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  has a multi-threaded and multi-processing Engine that quickly and efficiently sends and receives large volumes of messages.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Rock Solid
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is extremely reliable and has been engineered as Rock Solid Internet Software for sites where server down time cannot be tolerated.  
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Internet Standards
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is based on open standards and protocols of the Internet, and is completely interoperable with other Internet mail systems.  This means that }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  does not require a gateway to communicate with remote Internet e-mail servers.  }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is 100% compatible with the Internet RFC Standards for SMTP, POP3, IMAP4 and LDAP3.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Anti-Spam Security
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid16329650 Eudora}{\insrsid7218531  has integrated the acclaimed spam-scanning engine from Sophos into the }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail 3}{\insrsid7218531  server. }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail 3}{\insrsid7218531  uses a "cocktail" approach to spam filtering\'3b combining heuristics, profiles, keywords, white and black lists to offer very sensitive and accurate spam filtering. This approach offers the advantage of analyzing email and identifying spam during processing, before it is delivered to the users' inbox.
\par As the Sophos spam scanning engine analyzes messages, it calculates a spam score for each message based on techniques such as pattern matching, spam definitions, and heuristic analysis. Regular updates to the spam engine heuristics ensure continued effectiveness against the changing tactics of spammers. The spam scores for each message can be used to determine how the message is handled by the system.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Anti-Virus Security
\par }\pard\plain \s35\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Virus Filter can automatically scan all incoming mail for the presence of viruses. This allows your mail system to block e-mail borne viruses before they enter your network. }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's virus scanning facility is provided by Kaspersky Labs, a leading developer of centrally managed security solutions for the mobile enterprise.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Message Filtering (Sieve rules)
\par }\pard\plain \s35\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 In addition to its anti-spam and anti-virus features, }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  includes }{\i\insrsid7218531 message filtering}{\insrsid7218531 . With filters, you can create sophisticated rules for handling incoming messages based on the contents of their headers, bodies, and attachments.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Directory Harvest Attack Prevention (DHAP)
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb40\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail 3}{\insrsid7218531  includes the ability to protect corporate data and further reducing spam by detecting directory harvest attacks and automatically dropping the harvester's connection and blacklisting the IP address for a configurable period of time.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 Spammers use directory harvest attacks to steal corporate directories from their victims. They use this information to make their subsequent spam attacks easier for themselves and more costly to recipients. In addition to the obvious spam problem, directory harvest attacks can cause performance degradation issues while the harvesting action is in progress. }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  now detects these attacks and automatically drops inbound harvest connections, and then denies future connections to the sender. This safeguards sensitive corporate data.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Choice of Any Internet Mail Client
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Because }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  adheres to Internet e-mail standards, your users can choose any desktop operating system and any POP3 or IMAP4 e-mail client to access their }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Windows and Web Management }{\insrsid14683656 Center}{\insrsid7218531 s
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  provides two Management }{\insrsid14683656 Center}{\insrsid7218531  interfaces for managing mailboxes and mail lists, providing flexibility for both local and remote administration.  These include a stand-alone application (Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 ) and a browser-based interface (Web }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 ), both of which can be used to create, modify, and delete mailboxes and mail lists.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Multi-Level Administration Privileges
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports multiple levels of administration.  In addition to the }{\i\insrsid7218531 server administrator}{\insrsid7218531 , who has access over all domains and mailboxes, you can assign }{\i\insrsid7218531 domain administrators}{\insrsid7218531 , who can manage only the mailboxes and mail lists in their domain.  The administration of mail lists can be delegated to }{\i\insrsid7218531 mail list moderators}{\insrsid7218531 , who can define parameters associated with their lists, moderate membership requests, and moderate the content of list postings.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Mailbox Self-Administration
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  also allows end users to modify certain information related to their mailboxes.  This allows each user to change their password, set delivery preferences, and enable a vacation message--all without requiring the help of the server administrator.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Custom Default Mailbox Properties
\par }\pard\plain \s35\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb40\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The configuration data associated with a mailbox are called mailbox properties. Common mailbox properties items include mailbox quota size, POP/IMAP/webmail access, or anti-virus and anti-spam scanning options. }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail 3}{\insrsid7218531  now provides the ability to customize these default mailbox properties to ideally suit customer implementation requirements.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Mailbox property defaults can be modified through a special mailbox named MailboxTemplate, which is automatically created and located in the default domain. All mailboxes properties that have not been explicitly set will inherit that property from the new MailboxTemplate. Changing a property in the MailboxTemplate mailbox can also change that same property for all mailboxes for which that property has not been explicitly set. 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Database Integration
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  allows you to access mailbox and mail list data stored in an ODBC database.  This allows you to authenticate email users against an existing user database, and to create mail lists whose membership is based on users in a database table}{\insrsid15811578 .}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Web-Based Mailbox Access
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid16389365 Eudora Web Client}{\insrsid7218531  provides end users with access to their }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox through a web browser from any computer on the Internet.  This allows your users to send and receive e-mail even if they are away from their own computers.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Wireless Mailbox Access
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid5533515 Eudora Connect}{\insrsid7218531  provides users with mailbox access through WAP-compatible wireless Internet devices, such as cell phones and personal digital assistants (PDAs).
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Fast Installation
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's Installation Wizard allows you to quickly and effortlessly install the application.  The }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Engine's services are installed as NT services, allowing them to be automatically started when the machine boots up.  You can also start these services at the conclusion of the installation without rebooting your server.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Powerful Integrated List Server
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  includes a }{\i\insrsid7218531 list server}{\insrsid7218531 , which allows groups of users--such as employees, customers, and discussion groups--to easily exchange messages.  A message sent to a }{\i\insrsid7218531 mail list}{\insrsid7218531  is quickly broadcast to all of its members, allowing users to distribute mail to multiple users by sending it to one e-mail address. }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's comprehensive list server features include multiple moderators, e-mail moderation, e-mail subscription, message size limitation, digest distributions, configurable welcome and goodbye messages, web-based message archiving, and powerful header editing macros.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Automatic Reply Facility }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Auto-reply}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Each }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox includes an optional }{\i\insrsid7218531 auto-reply message}{\insrsid7218531 , which defines a response that should be automatically sent to each user who sends a mail to the mailbox.  You can use the auto-reply feature to create mailboxes dedicated to providing frequently requested information, such as product literature, newsletters, and product support assistance.  Your users can also make use the auto-reply feature to set up an automatic response for when they are away from the office and unable to receive e-mail.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Integrated With Windows Account Passwords
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  allows you to create mailboxes that correspond to Windows users on your server system.  When an Windows mailbox is created, its password is automatically taken the Windows login password for the user, allowing your users to have a single password for your server.  When you change a user's Windows login password, the user's }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox immediately uses the new password.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Secure Logon
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 You can enhance security on your e-mail system by encrypting mailbox passwords (including NT User passwords) using the secure APOP }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  APOP}}}{\insrsid7218531 , AUTH }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  AUTH}}}{\insrsid7218531 , AUTHORIZE }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  AUTHORIZE}}}{\insrsid7218531  or SPA }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  SPA}}}{\insrsid7218531  protocols, which are all supported by }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Flexible Logging
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  includes flexible logging options that support extensive message tracking and error detection information.  You can direct logging information to a file, to a database, and to the NT Event Viewer.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Virtual Domains }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Virtual domains}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Domains,Virtual}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 You can configure a single }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  server to send and receive mail for multiple domains.  This allows your site to host e-mail for "virtual" domains.  Mailbox names need not be unique across domains, so you can use a particular mailbox name in each domain on your server.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Performance Monitoring
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Engine is fully integrated with the performance monitoring and security features of Windows NT.  All Engine services can be monitored with the NT Performance Monitor, which can be used to track information such as the number of active connections, the amount of message data received, and the number of failed POP/IMAP logins.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Flexible Mailbox Authentication
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 User login data can be authenticated in several ways, allowing you to integrate existing user databases into }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 .  Users can be authenticated against the NT user database, an ODBC database, or mailbox data stored in the NT registry.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Programmability
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 You can extend the capability of }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  using }{\i\insrsid7218531 agents }{\cs98\i\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Agents}}}{\insrsid7218531 , which are programs that are executed on individual e-mail messages that arrive for the server, for a particular mailbox, or for a particular mail list.  For example, you could use an agent to automatically scan all incoming messages for virus attachments, or to forward messages to your pager if they contain the word "emergency" in the subject header.  Agents are extremely flexible and allow you to build-in almost any message-processing functionality.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  WhatsNewinVersion61}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  What's New in Version 6.1}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  What's New in Version 6.1}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  What's New in Version }{\insrsid12221366 3.0}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Domain Forwarding Support
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The domain properties have been enhanced to make it easier to use }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  as an SMTP gateway to relay mail to and from other email servers. A new tab entitled "Relay Host" has been added to simplify the configuration of }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  as an Internet gateway. 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP) Support
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 DHCP is a protocol that provides a means to dynamically allocate IP addresses to computers on a local area network. The system administrator assigns a range of IP addresses to DHCP and each client computer on the LAN has its TCP/IP software configured to request an IP address from the DHCP server. The request and grant process uses a lease concept with a controllable time period. 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 In order to use DHCP with }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , the administrator must configure the DNS settings in Windows rather than adding a DomainNameServer via }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 . This is done by configuring the IP settings for the application server, nominating a DNS server and deciding whether the server is to be DHCP enabled.  No application specific configuration is required for }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to resolve DNS queries. There are no }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  user interface changes for DHCP support. DHCP is defined in RFC 2131. 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Enhanced Sieve Rules Wizard
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The Sieve Rules Wizard screen has been enhanced to include a checkbox for quarantine instead of relying on the name "Junk Mail" in the fileinto edit control. It is now also possible to insert spam score X-headers and tag subject headers at the Mailbox Delivery Script level. In previous versions of }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , this was only possible in Server Receive Scripts. This is particularly useful for system administrators who want to provide anti-spam services to a subset of their total }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  user population.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 IP Address Binding
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  services (POP, IMAP, SMTP, etc.) running on multi-homed hosts can now bind to specific IP addresses rather than binding to any available IP address.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Secure Messaging (TLS/SSL) over IMAP, POP, and SMTP Protocols
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Transport Layer Security (TLSv.1) is the new Internet Standard by the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) for authenticating and encrypting transmissions across open networks. TLS is the evolution of Netscape's Secure Sockets Layer (SSLv.3), the implementation standard universally accepted on the World Wide Web for authenticated and encrypted communication between clients and servers.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Kaspersky Labs Anti-Virus Filter
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Kaspersky Labs award winning anti-virus engine is now fully integrated with }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  with no additional application instalation or configuration required.  Automatic updates to both the engine and the virus definition files ensure maximum protection with minimum administration.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 UIDPLUS Support
