\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailboxes,Types}}}{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports }{\insrsid14885638 three}{\insrsid7218531  different types of mailboxes, depending on your license key: Registry Mailboxes, NT}{\insrsid14885638  Mailboxes, and Database Mailboxes}{\insrsid7218531 .}{\insrsid16532054 
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid4199776 {\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid4199776 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid11405926 \{bml boxregi.bmp\}}{\insrsid16532054  }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Registry Mailboxes}{\insrsid7218531  are local to }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  and do not have access to any other parts of your operating system.  The password and user configuration information is stored in the Registry.  Use Registry Mailboxes if your users will only use the server to send and receive mail.  This will limit their permission to mail and will definitely prevent them from accessing any other part of the operating system.\txne\line }{\insrsid4199776 
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid4199776 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid11405926 \{bml boxnti.bmp\}}{\insrsid7747670\charrsid7747670  }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 NT MailBoxes }{\insrsid7218531 are authenticated against the Windows NT User Database.  NT Users may have \txne\line access to other aspects of your NT system, such as part of the file system. The password is \txne\line maintained in the NT user Database.  Use this type of mailbox if you want your users to access other\txne\line components of your NT server, such as the file system.  This means that they can use the same user\txne\line name and password to red their mail that they use to log into the Windows network and connect to \txne\line the file system.
\par }{\b\f2\insrsid16532054 
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid4199776 \b\f2\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid4199776 \{bml boxdbi.bmp\}}{\b\f2\insrsid4199776\charrsid4199776  }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Database Mailboxes}{\insrsid7218531  are authenticated against a table in an ODBC database.  The password is maintained in the database table.  Your license key may not enable this mailbox type.  Use this type of mailbox if you have a database that stores all of your usernames and passwords and wish to authenticate against this database.}{\b\f2\insrsid16532054\charrsid16532054 
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid10833445 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  AddingMailboxes}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Adding Mailboxes}}}{\insrsid7218531  Adding Mailboxes
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailboxes,Creating}}}{\insrsid7218531 Before your users can send and receive mail with }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , you must create a mailbox for each user.  To create mailboxes from the }{\uldb\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\uldb\insrsid7218531  }{\uldb\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 MailSiteConsole}{\insrsid7218531  program, open the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Domains}{\insrsid7218531  folder, select one of the existing domain directories within it, and open that domain's }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Mailboxes}{\insrsid7218531  directory.
{\v0\par\v}To create a new mailbox, click on one of these buttons:
{\v0\par\v}
{\v0\par\v}}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 {{{\pict\picscalex100\picscaley100\piccropl0\piccropr0\piccropt0\piccropb0\picw1217\pich1164\picwgoal690\pichgoal660\wmetafile8\bliptag-2019197270\blipupi-96 }
{\v0\par\v}}}}{\insrsid7218531  Create a new }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Registry Mailbox}{\insrsid7218531  by selecting this button on the toolbar.  A }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 New Registry Mailbox}{\insrsid7218531  icon will be displayed and you can enter the name of the mailbox in the field next to the icon.
{\v0\par\v}}\pard \ql \tx0\li0\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 {{{\pict\picscalex100\picscaley100\piccropl0\piccropr0\piccropt0\piccropb0\picw1217\pich1164\picwgoal690\pichgoal660\wmetafile8\bliptag1452113908\blipupi-96 }
\par}}}{\insrsid7218531  Create a new }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 NT Mailbox}{\insrsid7218531  by selecting this button on the toolbar.  The }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Add NT User}{\insrsid7218531  form will be displayed.  NT Users are created through the User Manager program.  Select the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 User Manager}{\insrsid7218531  icon in the }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  program group to run this program.
\par 
\par }{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 {{{\pict\picscalex100\picscaley100\piccropl0\piccropr0\piccropt0\piccropb0\picw1217\pich1164\picwgoal690\pichgoal660\wmetafile8\bliptag-2142244885\blipupi-96 }
\par}}}{\insrsid7218531  Create a new }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Database Mailbox}{\insrsid7218531  by selecting this button on the toolbar.  The }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Add Database Mailbox}{\insrsid7218531  form will be displayed.  Your license key may not enable this mailbox type.
\par 
\par  Each }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox can have one or more aliases.  If you wish to create aliases for the user, click on the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Aliases Folder}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 AliasesPage}{\insrsid7218531 .
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  PostmasterMailboxes}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Postmaster Mailboxes}}}{\insrsid7218531  Postmaster Mailboxes }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Postmaster}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailboxes,Postmaster}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 In }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , a mailbox called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 postmaster}{\insrsid7218531  is created automatically in the default domain (this mailbox is not counted for licensing purposes.)  If you wish messages addressed to the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 postmaster}{\insrsid7218531  to go to a different address, you can use either the mail forwarding facility or the alias table to achieve this. 
\par Mail addressed to }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 postmaster@virtual.domain}{\insrsid7218531  will be delivered to }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 postmaster@default.domain}{\insrsid7218531 , unless a mailbox called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 postmaster}{\insrsid7218531  is created in the virtual domain.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  CatchallMailboxes}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Catchall Mailboxes}}}{\insrsid7218531  Catchall Mailboxes }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Catchall}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailboxes,Catchall}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The mailbox name }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 catchall}{\insrsid7218531  is special.  If the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 catchall}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox exists in the virtual domain }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 abc.com}{\insrsid7218531 , then incoming mail addressed to a non-existent mailbox, such as }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 unknown@abc.com}{\insrsid7218531 , will instead be delivered to the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 catchall@abc.com}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox.  If the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 catchall}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox does not exist in the virtual domain, the message will be delivered to the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 catchall}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox in the default domain, if it exists.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  ConvertingMailboxes}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Converting Mailboxes}}}{\insrsid7218531  Converting Mailboxes
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailboxes,Converting}}}{\insrsid7218531 As described above, there are four different types of }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailboxes. Although you will typically create mailboxes of one type, you can also convert your existing mailboxes to any of the four types. For example, as your user base grows, you may want to convert your Registry Mailboxes to Database Mailboxes.
\par To convert a mailbox from on type to another, use the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSBOX}{\insrsid7218531  utility. This utility includes options for listing mailboxes by type and changing the type of one or more mailboxes. For example, you can convert all of your existing Database Mailboxes to Registry Mailboxes by executing the following commands in the Command Prompt:
\par }\pard\plain \s52\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 msbox -list }{\insrsid10574812 mydomain}{\insrsid7218531 .com 2 > users.txt\txne\line msbox -plugin @users.txt 0
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 With these two commands, }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSBOX}{\insrsid7218531  generates a list of Database Mailboxes  (type }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 2}{\insrsid7218531 ) and saves the list to the file }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 users.txt}{\insrsid7218531 , and then converts each mailbox listed in this file to Registry Mailboxes (type }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 0}{\insrsid7218531 ). Refer to the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Utilities Appendix}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 MSBOX}{\insrsid7218531  for more information on }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSBOX}{\insrsid7218531 .
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  AutomaticMailHandling}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Automatic Mail Handling}}}{\insrsid7218531  Automatic Mail Handling
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  provides very powerful features for automatically handling incoming messages. This can be useful in a variety of circumstances.
\par The automatic mail handling features are set up on an individual mailbox basis.  These features include Automatic Reply and Automatic Forwarding.  These features are configured using the Mailbox AutoReply page in the }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  AutomaticReplyFacility}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Automatic Reply Facility}}}{\insrsid7218531  Automatic Reply Facility }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Auto-reply}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 You can configure }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to automatically reply to incoming messages for a specific mailbox.  The Auto Reply feature is set up on an individual mailbox basis.  To set up the auto reply feature for a particular mailbox, invoke the Properties form by double clicking on the appropriate icon in the Mailbox folder in the }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par The Automatic Reply feature can be useful in a variety of circumstances:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls137\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls137\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 You may wish to setup a mailbox for receiving sales inquiries for your corporation.  For instance, you can create a }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 sales}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox and configure }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to send an automatic reply that acknowledges receipt of the message and forwards the message to the appropriate destination.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls137\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls137\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 You may wish to setup special mail handling for a former employee.  For instance, you can configure }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to automatically reply to all messages for that employee with a new message with a forwarding address explaining that the person is no longer employed with your company.  You can also configure }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to automatically forward the messages to the former employee's new address.
