\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 To remove a mail list, use the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Delete}{\insrsid7218531  button in the Mail Lists Folder of the }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  CreatingaDigestList}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Creating a Digest List}}}{\insrsid7218531  Creating a Digest List
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Digest mail lists}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail lists,Digest}}}{\insrsid7218531 Suppose you've created a popular mailing list called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 cars}{\insrsid7218531 , which receives 10 or 20 messages per day. There may be people who would like to subscribe to the list, but don't want to receive every message the moment it is sent. You can set up a }{\i\insrsid7218531 digest}{\insrsid7218531  mail list (in this case, }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 cars-digest}{\insrsid7218531 ) which accumulates all the messages received in one day and sends them in a single message.
\par With }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , you create a digest mailing list that is associated with an existing }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mailing list. To do this, select the Mail List folder in the }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .  Select the domain containing the list you want to create a digest for, and use the normal list-creation mechanism to create a new mailing list.   Assign the same name as the existing list with the word }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 -digest}{\insrsid7218531  appended to it. So if you want to create a digest list for an existing list called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 discuss}{\insrsid7218531 , create a new list called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 discuss-digest}{\insrsid7218531 . The }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 -digest}{\insrsid7218531  postfix tells }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to treat the list specially.
\par As far as the mail list subscriber is concerned, the digest list can be subscribed to and unsubscribed from just like other mailing lists. For instance, to subscribe, the user would send a }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 JOIN}{\insrsid7218531  command }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 to discuss-digest-request@myco.com}{\insrsid7218531 .  Note that a digest mailing list must be in the same domain as the list that it digests.
\par You cannot submit messages to the digest list. Any attempt to do so will result in a non-delivery message being returned. Messages must be submitted to the main list (}{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 discuss@myco.com}{\insrsid7218531 ).
\par When you open the properties for a digest list in the }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 , you will find that there is an extra page called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Digest}{\insrsid7218531 . You can use this page to control the extra properties of the digest list.
\par In the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 List General Page}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ListGeneralPage}{\insrsid7218531 , you will find that the fields relating to list moderation have been disabled. This is because list moderation is not necessary for digests.
{\v0\par\v}Also in the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 List General Page}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ListGeneralPage}{\insrsid7218531 , the function of the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Maximum message size}{\insrsid7218531  field is slightly different for digest lists. If this is non-zero, then messages will be accumulated until the maximum size is reached, or the normal digest accumulation period is reached (whichever is sooner).
{\v0\par\v}If a mail list has a digest, you can use the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Members and digesters}{\insrsid7218531  radio button to specify that members of the list itself and members of the digest list may both submit messages to the list.
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailListProcessorCommands}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail List Processor Commands}}}{\insrsid7218531  Mail List Processor Commands
