\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailListDirectories}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail List Directories}}}{\insrsid7218531  Mail List Directories
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,Mail list}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail lists,Directories}}}{\insrsid7218531 When }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  receives a message addressed to a mail list in one of it's local domains, the message is temporarily delivered to an appropriate subdirectory under the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 lists}{\insrsid7218531  directory.
\par For example, suppose the mail spool directory is }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 C:\\}{\b\f2\insrsid6317884 Program Files\\}{\b\f2\insrsid2231627 QUALCOMM\\WorldMail}{\b\f2\insrsid6317884 \\}{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 SPOOL}{\insrsid7218531 .  }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will automatically create a subdirectory called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 lists}{\insrsid7218531 .  Inside this }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 lists}{\insrsid7218531  directory, there will be two subdirectories for each mail list in the default domain: one for messages to the list itself, and one for messages to the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 list-request}{\insrsid7218531  address.  Subdirectories will also be created for each virtual domain to contain the list directories for lists within those domains.  Thus, if there is a list called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 staff}{\insrsid7218531  in the default domain, and there is another list called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 chat}{\insrsid7218531  within the virtual domain }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 xyz.com}{\insrsid7218531 , then the directory structure would be:
\par }\pard\plain \s58\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\rtlgutter\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 C:\\}{\insrsid6317884 Program Files\\}{\insrsid2231627 QUALCOMM\\WorldMail}{\insrsid6317884 \\}{\insrsid7218531 SPOOL\\lists\txne\line C:\\}{\insrsid6317884 Program Files\\}{\insrsid2231627 QUALCOMM\\WorldMail}{\insrsid6317884 \\}{\insrsid7218531 SPOOL\\lists\\staff\txne\line C:\\}{\insrsid6317884 Program Files\\}{\insrsid2231627 QUALCOMM\\WorldMail}{\insrsid6317884 \\}{\insrsid7218531 SPOOL\\lists\\staff-request\txne\line C:\\}{\insrsid6317884 Program Files\\}{\insrsid2231627 QUALCOMM\\WorldMail}{\insrsid6317884 \\}{\insrsid7218531 SPOOL\\lists\\~xyz.com\txne\line C:\\}{\insrsid6317884 Program Files\\}{\insrsid2231627 QUALCOMM\\WorldMail}{\insrsid6317884 \\}{\insrsid7218531 SPOOL\\lists\\~xyz.com\\chat\txne\line C:\\}{\insrsid6317884 Program Files\\}{\insrsid2231627 QUALCOMM\\WorldMail}{\insrsid6317884 \\}{\insrsid7218531 SPOOL\\lists\\~xyz.com\\chat-request
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 These directories are created automatically by }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  as needed.  Note that domain subdirectories are preceded by a tilde (~), to distinguish them from list directories.  Mail list names may not contain a tilde.
\par Messages are only held briefly in these directories, so you will typically find them empty.  However, you may place certain files in these directories, which will affect how }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  deals with mail list messages.  Refer to the section on }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 List Messages}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ListMessagesPage}{\insrsid7218531  for details.
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailListContentModeration}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail List Content Moderation}}}{\insrsid7218531  Mail List Content Moderation
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Moderators}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail lists,Moderator}}}{\i\insrsid7218531 Content Moderation}{\insrsid7218531  is a feature that allows mail list moderators to approve or reject messages sent to a mail list.  This level of list administration requires that the user have an account in a local domain.  To enable this feature, select the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Moderator controls content}{\insrsid7218531  feature in the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 List General Page}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ListGeneralPage}{\insrsid7218531 .
{\v0\par\v}When a new mail list message arrives to }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , it will first be checked to see if its author may post to the list.  If the author does not have posting permission (}{\i\insrsid7218531 e.g.}{\insrsid7218531  if he is not a member of the mail list and the mail list is set to disallow posting by non-members), the message will be returned to the author with an appropriate rejection message.  If the author does have permission, delivery processing depends on whether content moderation is enabled for the list.
{\v0\par\v}If content moderation is enabled, then the message will be placed in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 pending}{\insrsid7218531  directory for that list.  If content moderation is not enabled, then the message is placed directly into the mail list directory.  List messages will remain in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 pending}{\insrsid7218531  directory until one of the mail list moderators logs in to the Web }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  and select the Review page to review pending messages.  Messages may be reviewed, and rejected, accepted or discarded where appropriate.
{\v0\par\v}}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 Refer to the section on the }{\uldb\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 Web }{\uldb\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\v\uldb\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 WebListModeration}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531  for more information.
