\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Aliases,Wildcard}}}{\insrsid7218531 You can specify wildcards in the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Map from}{\insrsid7218531  field. This can be used to redirect mail for all names matching a pattern. For instance, specifying }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 T*Y}{\insrsid7218531  would match }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Tony}{\insrsid7218531 , }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Tiny}{\insrsid7218531 , }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 toby}{\insrsid7218531 , }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 terry}{\insrsid7218531 , etc. (Note that matching is not case sensitive.)
\par You can also specify a single wildcard as the first character of the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Map to}{\insrsid7218531  field. This will be replaced by the actual addressee's name when the table entry is used. For instance, if the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Map from}{\insrsid7218531  is }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 f*}{\insrsid7218531  and the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Map to}{\insrsid7218531  is }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 *-blue@abc.com}{\insrsid7218531 , then a message for }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 fargle@thismachine.mycompany.com}{\insrsid7218531  will be redirected to }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 fargle-blue@abc.com}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  Maptableorder}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Map table order}}}{\insrsid7218531  Map table order
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The order of entries in the map table is significant. It is processed top-to-bottom, and the first matching entry is used.  Thus, more specific entries (}{\i\insrsid7218531 i.e.}{\insrsid7218531  those not containing wildcards) should be positioned near the top of the list, and less specific entries (those containing wildcards) towards the end of the list. Use the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Up}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\insrsid7218531 Down}{\insrsid7218531  buttons to move entries around.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  ImportingandExporting}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Importing and Exporting}}}{\insrsid7218531  Importing and Exporting
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The list of aliases may be exported and imported to and from text files using the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Export}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\insrsid7218531 Import}{\insrsid7218531  buttons.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  AliasesversusSynonymDomains}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Aliases versus Synonym Domains}}}{\insrsid7218531  Aliases versus Synonym Domains
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Synonym domains}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Domains,Synonyms}}}{\insrsid7218531 Synonym domains are discussed in the preceding section.  There is some similarity between synonym domains and aliases.  For example, an alias of the form
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls13\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls13\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 *@xyzcompany.com -> *@xyz.com 
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 has the same effect as a synonym of }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 xyzcompany.com}{\insrsid7218531  for the virtual domain }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 xyz.com}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par The advantage of using synonym domains comes when you need to use aliases }{\i\insrsid7218531 in addition}{\insrsid7218531  to them.  For example, if you have synonyms of }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 abccompany.com}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 abcinc.com}{\insrsid7218531  for the virtual domain }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 abc.com}{\insrsid7218531 , you can alias an individual user (say }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 jim@abc.com}{\insrsid7218531 ) to another address using a single entry in the alias table such as:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls14\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls14\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 jim@abc.com -> james.smith@abc.com 
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 Because synonym domains affect aliases the same way that they do mailboxes, the addresses }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 jim@abccompany.com}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 jim@abcinc.com}{\insrsid7218531  are synonymous with the alias }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 jim@abc.com}{\insrsid7218531  shown above. 
\par }\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  DeliveryPrecedence}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Delivery Precedence}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Delivery Precedence}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Delivery Precedence
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  delivers messages to destination recipients based on an address precedence order.  }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  matches the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 To:}{\insrsid7218531  address in this order:
\par 1. Aliases }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Aliases}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par 2. Mail Lists
\par 3. Mailboxes
\par If a match is not found among these address types, the message will be delivered to a }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 catchall }{\cs98\b\f2\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Catchall}}}{\b\f2\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\b\f2\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailboxes,Catchall}}}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox (if one exists), or rejected by }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 . The following diagram illustrates these delivery precedence rules in action:
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid7154297 \{bmc precedence.bmp\}}{\insrsid7154297  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid7154297 
\par }\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  IntermittentConnectivity}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Intermittent Connectivity}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Intermittent Connectivity}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Intermittent Connectivity
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports mail servers that do not have a full time Internet connection.  This is useful in two situations:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid15275290 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid15275290 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls15\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls15\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is used as a central mail hub for dialup satellite mail servers.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid15275290 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid15275290 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls15\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls15\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  is used as a satellite mail server with a dialup connection to an ISP or a central hub.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  CentralHubwithDialupSatelliteServers}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Central Hub with Dialup Satellite Servers}}}{\insrsid7218531  Central Hub with Dialup Satellite Servers
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Dialup connectivity}}}{\insrsid7218531 The SMTP Receiver supports the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 ETRN }{\cs98\b\f2\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  ETRN}}}{\insrsid7218531  command, defined in RFC 1985, which allows a remote client to request delivery of mail queued for it's domain.  The }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSSTART }{\cs98\b\f2\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  MSSTART}}}{\insrsid7218531  utility connects to a mail server and uses the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 ETRN}{\insrsid7218531  command to initiate a mail download.  An intermittently connected satellite server can initiate delivery of mail queued for its domain by establishing a TCP/IP connection and then running }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSSTART}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  DialupSatelliteServer}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Dialup Satellite Server}}}{\insrsid7218531  Dialup Satellite Server
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can be configured to dialup to the central hub on a predefined schedule.  Once connected, }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can deliver any queued outgoing mail and can trigger delivery of any queued incoming mail.
\par Delivery of incoming mail can be triggered in one of two ways:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls16\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls16\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 If the central hub is configured as a SMTP relay for the satellite, and it supports the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 ETRN}{\insrsid7218531  command, then the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSSTART}{\insrsid7218531  command will trigger incoming delivery.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls16\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls16\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 If the central hub is configured to deliver all mail for the domain into a single POP mailbox, then the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSPOP }{\cs98\b\f2\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  MSPOP}}}{\insrsid7218531  command will pickup the mail and redistribute it to local mailboxes.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 The dialup schedule and the incoming delivery trigger are set in the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Time Of Day }{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 TimeofDaySchedule}{\insrsid7218531 window in the }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .  A batch file can be run as the incoming delivery trigger if }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSSTART}{\insrsid7218531  or }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSPOP}{\insrsid7218531  must be executed multiple times.
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailDeliverySchedules}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail Delivery Schedules}}}{\insrsid7218531  Mail Delivery Schedules
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Schedules}}}{\insrsid7218531 When }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  attempts to deliver a message to a foreign domain (}{\i\insrsid7218531 i.e.}{\insrsid7218531  a domain other than the default domain or a virtual domain), it may encounter a number of problems.  For example, the mail server for that domain may be down or otherwise temporarily inaccessible, or the server may not have enough disk space for the message.
\par A temporary delay of this nature will not cause the message to be treated as undeliverable.  Instead, }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will store the message on disk (in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 holding}{\insrsid7218531  directory), and try again at some later time.  Eventually, if the message still cannot be transmitted after a reasonable time, it will be treated as undeliverable.  The }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Delivery Schedule Management}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ScheduleManagement}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Delivery Schedule Management}}}{\insrsid7218531 tells }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  when to attempt delivery of such stored messages.
\par }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports two types of mail delivery schedules:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls17\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls17\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 The }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Elapsed Time Schedule}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ElapsedTimeSchedule}{\insrsid7218531 . }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Elapsed Time Schedule}}}{\insrsid7218531   Under this schedule, attempts to contact a domain will be made at a series of pre-configured intervals, commencing from the time at which the message was received.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls17\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls17\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 The }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Time-Of-Day Schedule}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 TimeofDaySchedule}{\insrsid7218531 . }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Time of Day Schedule}}}{\insrsid7218531   Under this schedule, attempts to contact a domain will be made at specific, configurable, times of day.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 You can control which destination domains use which kind of schedule. You can also force all domains to use Time-Of-Day Schedule by specifying }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 !*}{\insrsid7218531  in the Delivery Schedule Management dialog.
\par The elapsed time schedule is ideal when }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  has a continuous, uninterrupted connection to the Internet.  The time-of-day schedule is more appropriate when the Internet connection is intermittent - typically, a dialup connection.
\par You can also request }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to attempt immediate delivery of all messages for one or more domains.
\par }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can manage a dialup connection for you, if you so wish.  Refer to the next section for more information. 
\par Mail delivery schedules are managed through the Schedules Folder in the Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .  Refer to }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Schedule Management}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ScheduleManagement}{\insrsid7218531  in the Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  Reference section for more information.
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  DialupSupport}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Dialup Support}}}{\insrsid7218531  Dialup Support
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports dialup connectivity to the Internet through the Microsoft Remote Access Service (RAS).  This allows a computer running }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to dial into an Internet Service Provider (ISP) to exchange mail on a predetermined schedule.
\par In order to use the dialup support, you must install RAS.  See the Microsoft documentation concerning RAS installation.  You will need to create at least one RAS phonebook entry, containing the phone number of your ISP.  Before configuring the dialup support in }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , check the basic RAS setup by dialing out to your ISP using the Dialup Networking tool provided with RAS.  If this does not work, }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will not be able to dial out.
\par Dialup support in }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  works like this:  At regular intervals (which you can configure), }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  dials your ISP.  Once connected, it will execute a command to request the ISP's mail server to send mail to }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 .  It will also attempt to deliver outgoing mail through the normal }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  mail routing mechanism (i.e. the DNS and the manual routing table).  If you wish, you can configure the manual routing table such that all outgoing mail is routed to your ISP's mail server for it to forward--this may help reduce the time spent connected.  When there is no more outgoing mail to send, and there are no incoming connections, the dialup connection will be closed and the phone disconnected.
\par Refer to }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Schedule Management}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ScheduleManagement}{\insrsid7218531  in the Windows }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  Reference section for more information.
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  Backup}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Backup}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Backup}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Backup
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  PerformingaComprehensiveBackup}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Performing a Comprehensive Backup}}}{\insrsid7218531  Performing a Comprehensive Backup
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Backup}}}{\insrsid7218531 To perform a comprehensive backup of your }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  post office, you need to save several components:
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  RegistryConfiguration}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Registry Configuration}}}{\insrsid7218531  Registry Configuration
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 When run with the Registry connector (the default mode), }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  stores all of its settings in the Windows Registry of your server.
\par }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  comes with a utility, }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSBACK}{\insrsid7218531 , that you can use to backup your registry configuration data to a text file.  This file can then be included in your backup schedule.  We highly recommend that you run this command in your daily backup script.  Refer to the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Utilities Appendix}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 MSBACK}{\insrsid7218531  for more information on }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSBACK}{\insrsid7218531 .
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  SpooledMailMessages}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Spooled Mail Messages}}}{\insrsid7218531  Spooled Mail Messages }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,Spool}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 These files are located in the directories specified in the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Directories}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 DirectoriesPage}{\insrsid7218531  dialog in the }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .  All of these directories, together with any lower level directories, should be included in your backup schedule.
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailboxDirectories}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailbox Directories}}}{\insrsid7218531  Mailbox Directories }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailbox directories}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,Mailboxes}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 These directories store e-mail messages for the mailboxes on your system, and are located in the mailbox root directory for each domain.  The mailbox directory is defined in the General page of the Domain Properties window.  All mailbox directories should be included in your backup schedule.
