\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 All SSL/TLS security settings are available via the TLS tab of the Security Properties window. }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  allows you to specify the level of TLS deployment separately for each of the three mail protocols}{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  SMTP, POP3, and IMAP4. Each protocol has a separate area within the window. All three protocols use the same drop-down menu settings.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 SMTP Protocol
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 When receiving SMTP connections, the settings available from the drop-down menu are:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls156\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls156\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Disable TLS (default) }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  communicates in clear text mode.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls156\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls156\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Allow TLS }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  negotiates with the mail client and optionally encrypts messages if the client has SSL/TLS configured.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls156\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls156\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Require TLS }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  forces messages to be encrypted.
\par }\pard\plain \s35\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx1440\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 When the "Allow TLS" setting is selected, you must specify how mail will be sent when using SMTP. The two settings available from that drop-down menu are:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls157\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls157\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Use TLS if available }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  optionally encrypts messages.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls157\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls157\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Require TLS is supported }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  forces the client to encrypt messages, but only if the client software supports TLS.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 POP3 Protocol and IMAP4 Protocol
\par }\pard\plain \s35\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The POP3 and IMAP4 Protocol areas of the Security Properties window provide the same configuration setting choices. To limit redundancy, they are described together in this subsection.  
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx1440\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 When receiving POP3 connections or IMAP4 connections, the settings available from the drop-down menu are:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls156\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls156\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Disable TLS (default) }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  communicates in clear text mode.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls156\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls156\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Allow TLS }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  negotiates with the mail client and optionally encrypts messages if the client has SSL/TLS configured.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls156\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls156\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Require TLS }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  forces messages to be encrypted.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx1440\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 Two checkboxes may also be set:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls158\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls158\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Disable Plain Text Logins }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  Checking this box forces the client to encrypt login details (when both the server and client have agreed to use SSL/TLS).
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls158\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls158\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Enable alternate SSL port }{\insrsid7218531 {\field{\*\fldinst SYMBOL 190 \\f "Symbol" \\s 8}{\fldrslt\f3\fs16\'be}}}{\insrsid7218531  Checking this box supports the use of an alternate secure port (this feature is required when the client software supports SSL 3.0 but not TLS 1.0). The alternate port number must be entered in the adjacent text box.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailFilters}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Mail Filters}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail Filters}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Mail Filters
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail Filters}}}{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  includes support for }{\i\insrsid7218531 mail filters}{\insrsid7218531 . Filters are rules for mail handling that allow you to specify that messages should be handled in special ways - for instance, forwarded to a specific email address, saved to the file system, or rejected - based on characteristics of the message. Filters are especially useful for identifying messages that may contain email viruses and preventing them from entering your system.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  FilterLevels}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Filter Levels}}}{\insrsid7218531  Filter Levels
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports mail content filters at three different levels:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\listtextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls148\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0 {\b\insrsid7218531 Server filters}{\insrsid7218531 , which are applied to every message received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's SMTP server.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\listtextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\b\insrsid7218531 Domain filters}{\insrsid7218531 , which apply only to messages sent to or from a mailbox in a specific domain.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\listtextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\b\insrsid7218531 Mailbox filters}{\insrsid7218531 , which apply only to messages sent to or from a specific mailbox.
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 For all three types, the user }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  interface described in this section can be used by the administrator to create, modify, and delete filter rules. Mailbox filters can also be defined by end users through the }{\insrsid16389365 Eudora Web Client}{\insrsid7218531  interface.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  UsingFilters}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Using Filters}}}{\insrsid7218531  Using Mail Filters
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 To use mail filters, open the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Security}{\insrsid7218531  folder in the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  and double-click }{\b\insrsid7218531 Sieve Filter}{\insrsid7218531 . This displays the Sieve Filter Rules window, which lists the sever-level content filters currently defined on your site.  An identical window for managing domain filters can be accessed by clicking the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Sieve Filter}{\insrsid7218531  icon within the domain's folder in the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid12480280 \{bmc filter2.bmp\}}{\insrsid12480280  }{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531\charrsid12480280 
\par }{\insrsid7218531 The rules defined in this list are applied sequentially, so if a message is rejected by an initial filter it will not be subject to subsequent rules. You can move filters up and down in this list to refine your filtering strategies. To create a new filter rule click }{\b\insrsid7218531 New}{\insrsid7218531 , which launches the Rule Wizard.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  NameAndDescription}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Name and Description}}}{\insrsid7218531  Name and Description
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Rule Wizard }}}{\insrsid7218531 The first panel of the Rule Wizard defines the name and description of your new filter rule. Both the name and description of each filter appears in the Sieve Filter Rules window.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid12480280 \{bmc filter3.bmp\}}{\insrsid12480280  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid12480280 
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Filter names must be unique and can be contain up to 30 characters. When you finish entering your filter rule's name and description, click }{\b\insrsid7218531 Next}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  AddingFilterCriteria}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Adding Filter Criteria}}}{\insrsid7218531  Adding Filter Criteria
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The next panel of the Rule Wizard displays the filtering criteria for your filter rule. These are the conditions that will cause a message to be subject to the filter rule. 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid12480280 \{bmc filter4.bmp\}}{\insrsid12480280  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid12480280 
\par }{\insrsid7218531 By default, a message must match }{\i\insrsid7218531 all}{\insrsid7218531  of the criteria defined in this list to be subject to the filter rule.  You can modify this behavior to filter messages that match }{\i\insrsid7218531 any}{\insrsid7218531  of the given criteria by selecting the appropriate option at the top of this panel.  To add criteria to your filter rule, click }{\b\insrsid7218531 Add}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 To define filter criteria, select the part of the message that you want to search and the text string for which you are searching. You can also use regular expressions to define sophisticated text searches.
\par }\pard\plain \s35\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 When defining filtering criteria, you can search for the given text in either the headers (From, Subject, To, Cc, Bcc, Sender, Reply-To, etc.) or body of the message. You can also test for the existance of a header, as well as for the size of the entire message (including headers, body, and all attachments). To search in a header not given shown in the menu, click in the menu value and enter the header you wish to search. Attachments are considered part of the message body, so when searching for attachment content select }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 <Message Body>}{\insrsid7218531 . 
\par For example, to filter messages that contain the attachment }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 virus.vbs}{\insrsid7218531 , use the following criteria:
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid12480280 \{bmc sieve filter - new criterion 256c.bmp\}}{\insrsid12480280  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid12480280 
\par }\pard\plain \s35\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 To specify a regular expression search, enable the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Regular Expression}{\insrsid7218531  option. This also enables a }{\b\insrsid7218531 Test}{\insrsid7218531  button that allows you to test your regular expression syntax on sample message content. See the following section on }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Advanced Filter Options}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 AdvancedFilterOptions}{\insrsid7218531  for more information.
{\v0\par\v}After you have finished adding criteria for your filter rule, click }{\b\insrsid7218531 Next}{\insrsid7218531 .
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  SetAFilterAction}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Set a Filter Action}}}{\insrsid7218531  Set a Filter Action
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The next panel of the Rule Wizard defines the action to be taken against messages that satisfy the criteria for the filter rule. In other words, if a message contains the characteristics that you set for this rule, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will handle that message according to the actions you set here.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid12480280 \{bmc sieve filter - modify rule 256c.bmp\}}{\insrsid12480280  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid12480280 
\par }\pard\plain \s35\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 You can specify that messages caught by your filter rule should be rejected, forwarded, saved to a given file system directory, or any combination of the above. If the message is not rejected, you can also choose whether or not the message should be delivered to its intended recipients. 
\par The choices you should make here are dependent on the type of filter rule you are creating. For example, if your filter rule scans for messages that have virus attachments, you will probably want to reject any such messages\'3b if your filter rule archives urgent messages sent to the postmaster, you should save copies of these messages and also allow normal delivery.
\par Note that the actions available in this panel change slightly when creating domain or mailbox filters. For domain filters, copying a message to a file is not available. For mailbox filters, a message can only be copied to a folder within the recipient's mailbox folder.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  TestingFilters}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Testing Filters}}}{\insrsid7218531  Testing Filters
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 After you have created filter rules you can test their behavior on sample messages. Testing filter rules is important to verify the affect that they will have on your site's mail activity, and to confirm that they work as intended.
\par To test your filter rules, open the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Sieve Filter Rules}{\insrsid7218531  window and click }{\b\insrsid7218531 Test}{\insrsid7218531 . The following window is displayed:
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid10889022 \{bmc sieve filter - test rule2 - 256c.bmp\}}{\insrsid10889022  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid10889022 
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Filter tests are run against all messages in a specific directory. Use the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Browse}{\insrsid7218531  button to select a test message directory, such as an existing mailbox. If you have created filter rules to screen out specific viruses, be sure that your test directory includes messages that include the targeted viruses. You should also test your filters against "normal" messages to insure that the filters do not catch them by mistake.
\par After you select a message directory, click }{\b\insrsid7218531 Run}{\insrsid7218531 . This will cause your filtering rules to be applied to the messages in this directory exactly as if they are incoming messages. If a message is subject to a filter rule, then this window displays the name of the message file, the filter rule that applies to it, and the action(s) taken against the message. The possible actions are }{\b\insrsid7218531 Reject}{\insrsid7218531  (message blocked), }{\b\insrsid7218531 Forward}{\insrsid7218531  (message forwarded to the given address), }{\b\insrsid7218531 Copy}{\insrsid7218531  (copy of the message is saved), }{\b\insrsid7218531 Discard}{\insrsid7218531  (message is not delivered to its recipients), and }{\b\insrsid7218531 Stop}{\insrsid7218531  (no more filter rules are applied to the message). If a message is shown with no rule or action, then that message would be delivered normally.
\par The order of entries in the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Filter Rules}{\insrsid7218531  window is significant: rules are applied in the order that they appear in this list. This means that if the first filter rejects a message (}{\b\insrsid7218531 Reject}{\insrsid7218531 ), or specifies that additional filter rules should not be applied to it (}{\b\insrsid7218531 Stop}{\insrsid7218531 ), then the remaining filter rules are irrelevant for that message. It is therefore important to test your general filtering strategy, not just individual filter rules. Move entries up and down in the rules list to fine-tune mail filtering on your site.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 
