31 
\par }\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  VirusScanning}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Virus Scanning}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Virus Scanning}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Virus Scanning
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Virus scanning}}}{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  includes support for integrated }{\i\insrsid7218531 virus scanning}{\insrsid7218531 .  These features allow }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to identify messages that have potentially destructive virus content and block them before they enter your network.  When virus scanning is enabled and a message that contains a virus is received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , it will reject the message and inform the sender of the infection.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  KasperskyAntiVirus}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Kaspersky Anti Virus}}}{\insrsid7218531  Kaspersky Anti-Virus Filter
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's virus scanning engine is provided by the Kaspersky Labs.  This is integrated into }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , and so no configuration of the engine is required for use with }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  VirusScanningPolicies}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Virus Scanning Policies}}}{\insrsid7218531  Virus Scanning Policy
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports three different virus-scanning policies:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\listtextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls148\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0 {\b\insrsid7218531 Server-level virus scanning}{\insrsid7218531 , which causes every message received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 ' SMTP server to be scanned for viruses.  This policy is typically used by offices, universities, and other organizations.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\listtextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\b\insrsid7218531 Domain-level virus scanning}{\insrsid7218531 , which specifies that messages should be scanned for viruses only if they are sent to or from a mailbox in specific domains.  This policy is typically used by mail hosting companies that wish to sell virus scanning as a value-added feature for hosted domains.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\listtextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\b\insrsid7218531 Mailbox-level virus scanning}{\insrsid7218531 , which specifies that messages should be scanned for viruses only if they are sent to or from specific mailboxes.  This policy is typically used by ISPs that wish to sell virus scanning as a value-added feature for their subscribers.
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Note that the domain and mailbox virus scanning policies can be used together. This means that you can configure virus scanning to occur for all mailboxes in one domain, while scanning only for selected mailboxes in a second domain.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  ServerVirusScanning}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Server Virus Scanning}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Server Virus Scanning}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  Server Virus Scanning
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 To configure }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's virus scanning policies, open the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  and double-click the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Kaspersky Anti-Virus Filter}{\insrsid7218531  icon in the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Security}{\insrsid7218531  folder. This displays the Virus Scanning Filter window:
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid7218531 {\object\objautlink\rsltpict\objw6526\objh7741{\*\objclass }{\*\objdata }{\result {\insrsid5271419 {\*\shppict{\pict\picscalex100\picscaley100\piccropl0\piccropr0\piccropt0\piccropb0\picw11509\pich13653\picwgoal6525\pichgoal7740\pngblip\bliptag1086049836 }}{\nonshppict{\pict\picscalex100\picscaley100\piccropl0\piccropr0\piccropt0\piccropb0\picw11508\pich13654\picwgoal6524\pichgoal7741\wmetafile8\bliptag1086049836\blipupi95 }}}}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par The option }{\b\insrsid7218531 Enable virus scanning on this mail server}{\insrsid7218531  controls the global virus scanning policy.  If this option is disabled, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will not scan any messages.  Otherwise, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will scan messages according to the other settings here.
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 If you want to protect all users on your site from viruses and scan every incoming message, select }{\b\insrsid7218531 Scan all messages received by SMTP}{\insrsid7218531 . When this option is selected, all mail received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's SMTP server will be scanned for viruses regardless of sender or destination.
\par If you want to instead use domain or mailbox-level virus scanning, select }{\b\insrsid7218531 Scan all messages sent by or to enabled mailboxes/domains}{\insrsid7218531 .  When this option is selected, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will scan mail based on the virus scanning preferences of the sender or recipient domains on your site.
\par }\pard \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 When the virus scanner fails or is down, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can be configured to defer or accept messages.
\par The maximum time allowed for a scan is configurable in milliseconds.
\par When a scan times out, we can accept, reject or defer the message.
\par The SMTP server's response when rejecting a message due to a timeout can be set.
\par Some viruses are transmitted via password protected archives which are encrypted and can not be scanned by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 .  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can be set to reject messages containing password protected archives by treating them as unsafe or to accept by treating them as safe.
\par }\pard \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 Included in the Virus Scanning Filter window are controls for downloading updated virus definition files, which are needed for }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to block new viruses as they are discovered. By default, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  polls once an hour for updates to virus definition files.  You can force an immediate update by clicking }{\b\insrsid7218531 Update now}{\insrsid7218531 . Note that your license may not support virus updates\'3b in this case, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will automatically disable polling for updates.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  DomainVirusScanning}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Domain Virus Scanning}}}{\insrsid7218531  Domain Virus Scanning
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 To configure domain virus scanning options, open the domain folder in the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  double-click the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Kaspersky Anti-Virus Filter}{\insrsid7218531  icon. This displays the Virus Scanning Filter window:
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid11929355 \{bmc virus scanning - domain - 256c.bmp\}}{\insrsid11929355  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid11929355 
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The option }{\b\insrsid7218531 Enable virus scanning on messages to or from this domain}{\insrsid7218531  controls the virus scanning policy for this domain.  If this option is disabled, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will not scan any messages sent to or from this domain.  Otherwise, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will scan messages according to the other settings here.
\par If you want virus scanning to occur for all users in the domain, select }{\b\insrsid7218531 Scan all messages}{\insrsid7218531 . When this option is selected, all mail received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's SMTP server that is sent to or from a mailbox within this domain will be scanned.
\par If you want to instead use mailbox-level virus scanning, select }{\b\insrsid7218531 Scan messages sent to/from enabled mailboxes}{\insrsid7218531 .  When this option is selected, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will scan mail based on the virus scanning preferences of the sender or recipient mailbox.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailboxVirusScanning}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailbox Virus Scanning}}}{\insrsid7218531  Mailbox Virus Scanning
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 To configur}{\insrsid11929355 e}{\insrsid7218531  mailbox virus scanning, open the mailbox in the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  and select the Security tab:
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid10833445 \{bmc virus scanning - mailbox - 256c.bmp\}}{\insrsid10833445  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid10833445 
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The }{\b\insrsid7218531 Enable virus scanning on all mail to or from this mailbox}{\insrsid7218531  controls virus scanning for the individual mailbox.  When this option is enabled, messages received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's SMTP server will be virus scanned if they are sent to or from this mailbox.  If disabled, no virus scanning occurs for this mailbox. Note that this field will be disabled if the server or domain virus scanning policies are not configured for mailbox-level scanning.
\par }\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  hSpamScanning}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Spam Scanning}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Spam Scanning}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Spam Scanning
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  includes support for integrated }{\i\insrsid7218531 spam scanning}{\insrsid7218531 .  These features allow }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to determine how likely it is that a given message is spam. Customers can then take appropriate action using sieve scripts. Typically, messages likely to be spam are delivered to a "bulk mail" folder.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Sophos Anti-Spam Filter
\par }\pard\plain \s35\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's spam scanning engine is provided by Sophos. This is integrated into }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , and so no configuration of the engine is required for use with }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa100\saauto1\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  SpamScanningPolicy}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Spam Scanning Policy}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Spam Scanning Policy}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  Spam Scanning Policy
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports three different spam-scanning policies. If spam scanning is enabled, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  scans appropriate messages as they arrive, and it is the associated sieve scripts that determine the action taken. Scanning can be enabled at three levels:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\listtextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\jclisttab\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls148\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0 {\b\insrsid7218531 Server-level spam scanning}{\insrsid7218531 , which causes every message received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 ' SMTP server to be scanned for potential spam.  This policy is typically used by offices, universities, and other organizations.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\listtextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\b\insrsid7218531 Domain-level spam scanning}{\insrsid7218531 , which specifies that messages should be scanned for spam only if they are sent to or from a mailbox in specific domains.  This policy is typically used by mail hosting companies that wish to sell spam scanning as a value-added feature for hosted domains.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\listtextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\b\insrsid7218531 Mailbox-level spam scanning}{\insrsid7218531 , which specifies that messages should be scanned for spam only if they are sent to or from specific mailboxes.  This policy is typically used by ISPs that wish to sell spam scanning as a value-added feature for their subscribers.
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Note that the domain and mailbox spam scanning policies can be used together. This means that you can configure spam scanning to occur for all mailboxes in one domain, while scanning only for selected mailboxes in a second domain.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Taking Action On Spam with Sieve Filters
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 While the Sophos spam-scanning engine provides the power to determine how likely it is that a given message is spam, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's enhanced Sieve rule implementation provides administrators and end-users alike the power to implement and enforce their own personal spam policy. Actions include: reject, redirect, annotate, quarantine, and deliver. 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Spam Quarantine
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Rather than immediately discarding or rejecting messages suspected of being spam, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  administrators have the option of sending these messages to a special spam quarantine folder which is automatically created for each user and is located in each users mailbox. 
\par End-users can periodically review their spam quarantine folder to identify any false positives, which may be eliminated through a whitelisting process. This "Junk Mail" folder can be reviewed by end-users through }{\insrsid16389365 Eudora Web Client}{\insrsid7218531  or any standard IMAP email client.
\par End-users can also implement their own policy for sending messages to the spam quarantine. This special quarantine folder automatically purges messages every 30 days in order to avoid any over-quota concerns.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Personal Whitelisting
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 A white list is a list of addresses of trusted senders whose messages are delivered unchecked. The white list can be used to recognize mailing list traffic and opt-in marketing messages that might otherwise be classified as spam. With }{\insrsid15275290 WorldMail 3}{\insrsid7218531 , end-users can create and manage their own personal white lists, thus relieving the system administrator of this task. 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa100\saauto1\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid16329217 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  eServerSpamScanning}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Server Spam Scanning}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Server Spam Scanning}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  Server Spam Scanning
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 To configure }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's spam scanning policies, open the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  and double-click the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Sophos Anti-Spam Filter}{\insrsid7218531  icon in the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Security}{\insrsid7218531  folder. This displays the Spam Scanning Filter window:
\par }\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb240\sa240\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\pard\plain \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb240\sa240\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid10833445 \{bmc spam scanning - server - 256c.bmp\}}{\insrsid10833445  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid10833445 
\par }\pard \s30\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 The option }{\b\insrsid7218531 Enable spam scanning on this mail server}{\insrsid7218531  controls the global spam scanning policy.  If this option is not selected, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will not scan any messages.  Otherwise, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will scan messages according to the other settings here.
\par }{\b\ul\insrsid7218531 Note}{\insrsid7218531 : }{\i\insrsid7218531 Upon entering this dialog the following test will be performed.  If there are more mailboxes provisioned for Anti-Spam then there are licenses for, this option will be unchecked.  Upon exiting the dialog another test for this same condition is done.  If the licensed amount of mailboxes has been exceeded, then the user will be notified that this option will be turned off.
\par }{\insrsid7218531 If you want to protect all users on your site from spam and scan every incoming message, select }{\b\insrsid7218531 Process all messages received by SMTP}{\insrsid7218531 . When this option is selected, all mail received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's SMTP server will be scanned for spam regardless of sender or destination.
\par }{\b\ul\insrsid7218531 Note}{\insrsid7218531 : }{\i\insrsid7218531 If there are more mailboxes in the server than there are Anti-Spam licenses for, this option will be disabled.
\par }{\insrsid7218531 If you want to instead use domain or mailbox-level spam scanning, select }{\b\insrsid7218531 Process all messages sent by or to enabled mailboxes/domains}{\insrsid7218531 .  When this option is selected, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will scan mail based on the spam scanning preferences of the sender or recipient domains on your site.
\par By default, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will not scan messages of over 100KB for spam. Unsolicited mails are typically very small, but this value can be changed if required.
\par Included in the Spam Scanning Filter window are controls for downloading updated anti-spam heuristics files, which are needed for }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to block new forms of spam as they are discovered. By default, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  polls once an hour for updates to heuristics files.  You can force an immediate update by clicking }{\b\insrsid7218531 Update now}{\insrsid7218531 . 
\par Spam scanning can be forced on. This allows an administrator to monitor the level of spam passing through the system even if the license does not allow scanning.
