trbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \trbrdrh\brdrs\brdrw15 \trbrdrv\brdrs\brdrw15 \trftsWidth1\trpaddl108\trpaddr108\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth1620\clshdrawnil \cellx1980\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth6750\clshdrawnil \cellx8730\row }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 The message file (}{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 %f}{\insrsid7218531 ) will be located in the mail list directory, but will not have a }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSG}{\insrsid7218531  extension. The external program may change the message contents or delete the message file. When the external program completes, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will automatically rename the file (if it still exists) to have a }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSG}{\insrsid7218531  extension, and will process it as normal. 
\par Multiple commands can be executed by interposing the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 &}{\insrsid7218531  character between them, or by using a batch file.
\par The agent is executed by SMTPDA and therefore inherits the NT access rights of SMTPDA.  When the agent has finished executing then the message will be interpreted by the mail list processor.
\par It is important that the agent should not take too long to execute, since }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will not process any other mail list messages while it is running.
\par Mail list processor agents can be used to implement a wide range of features, including providing additional mail list processor commands.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  ArchiveAgent}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Archive Agent}}}{\insrsid7218531  Archive Agent
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Archiving,Messages}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Archive Agent}}}{\insrsid7218531 Unlike other agents, the Archive Agent is built in to the mail server.  Its purpose is to make a copy of every message received by the mail server.  The Archive Agent can help to satisfy the legal requirement to retain all e-mail sent by a company in some jurisdictions.
\par To enable the Archive Agent, click on the Agents icon in the Window }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 's Server folder, which displays the Agents dialog.  Enter the archive directory name in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Archive directory}{\insrsid7218531  field of this window.
\par The archive directory will be automatically created if it does not already exist.  Under this directory, the agent will create a new subdirectory each day for that day's messages.  The archive subdirectories will have a name of the form }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 YYYYMMDD}{\insrsid7218531 , where }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 YYYY}{\insrsid7218531  is the year, }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MM}{\insrsid7218531  is the month (01 to 12) and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 DD}{\insrsid7218531  is the day of the month (01 to 31).  The agent will copy each }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 RCP}{\insrsid7218531  file and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSG}{\insrsid7218531  file that is received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  into this directory.
\par Note that the agent will archive not only messages received by }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , but also messages generated by the mail server itself, such as delivery status notifications and messages expanded by the mail list processor.
\par }\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid8018829 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  Databases}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Databases}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Databases}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Databases
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Databases}}}{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can integrate with a relational database through ODBC (Open Database Connectivity).  }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can use a database for three things - mailbox authentication\'3b storing mail list membership\'3b and logging.  This chapter describes how }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can be configured to do this.
\par You must have ODBC drivers installed if you wish to use this feature. Note that you should not attempt to use this these features if you are not familiar with databases and their terminology.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  SettingUpDatabaseAccess}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Setting Up Database Access}}}{\insrsid7218531  Setting Up Database Access
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 If your ODBC database is running on a different machine than the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Engine, you may need to take additional setup steps. By default, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  services run as the Windows }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 SYSTEM}{\insrsid7218531  account, which can access to other machines only via TCP/IP. This means that if your database does not allow connections via TCP/IP, }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will not be able to access the database.
\par To enable database access between systems, you must do one of the following:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls142\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls142\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Configure your database to allow TCP/IP connections (refer to your database's documentation for instructions on doing this).
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls142\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls142\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 Change the account that the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  services run as from }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 SYSTEM}{\insrsid7218531  to an NT account that has access rights to the database. You can do this from the Services Control Panel.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  DatabaseMailboxPlugin}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Database Mailbox Plugin}}}{\insrsid7218531  Database Mailbox Plugin
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Plugins,Database mailbox}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Database Mailbox plugin}}}{\insrsid7218531 The database mailbox plugin allows you to base authentication on a database. You will find this useful if you have an existing database of users to whom you wish to offer mailbox facilities. Note that you should not attempt to use this plugin unless you are familiar with databases and their terminology.
\par To configure the database mailbox plugin, select the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Plugins Folder}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 MailboxPluginsFolder}{\insrsid7218531  in the }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  and double click on the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Database Mailbox Plugin}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 DatabaseMailboxPlugin}{\insrsid7218531 . The Database Mailbox Plugin supports two kinds of databases: Generic and Emerald Radius Server databases.
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  EmeraldDatabase}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Emerald Database}}}{\insrsid7218531  Emerald Database }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Emerald}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Information on using the Database Plugin with an Emerald Database is provided in the appendix on }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Emerald Integration}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 EmeraldIntegration}{\insrsid7218531 .
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  GenericDatabase}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Generic Database}}}{\insrsid7218531  Generic Database
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The Generic database assumes a very straightforward database schema. User information is contained in a single table, }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Mailboxes}{\insrsid7218531 , with columns }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Mailbox}{\insrsid7218531 , }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 FullName}{\insrsid7218531 , }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Password}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Domain}{\insrsid7218531 .  You can override these defaults by filling in the fields on the configuration form.
\par An example of using the Database Mailbox Plugin is provided in the appendix on }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Database Examples}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 DatabasePluginExamples}{\insrsid7218531 .
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  DatabaseMailListPlugin}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Database Mail List Plugin}}}{\insrsid7218531  Database Mail List Plugin
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Plugins,Database mail list}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Database Mail List plugin}}}{\insrsid7218531 The Database Mail List Plugin makes use of some default properties.  This makes it possible to create Database Mail Lists with minimal configuration.  For the default configuration, the following applies:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls139\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls139\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 An ODBC data source can be used for all domains. This will need to be entered into the Mail list properties in the Database Tab of the Database Mail List.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls139\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls139\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 A separate table is used for each mail list.\~ The name of the table must be the same as the name of the mail list, except that where the mail list name contains a dot or hyphen character.  If the list name contains a dot or hyphen you must create the table using the underscore character.\~ This is because dot and hyphen are not legal table name characters in some databases.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls139\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls139\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\insrsid7218531 The table must contain at least two columns, called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 EmailAddress}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 FullName.}{\insrsid7218531    These columns must contain the e-mail addresses and names of the mail list members.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 For example, create a database mailing list called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 customers}{\insrsid7218531  in the virtual domain }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 abc.com}{\insrsid7218531 .  The list address would be }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 customers@abc.com}{\insrsid7218531 .\~ To map this to a database, create a data source called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 abc.com}{\insrsid7218531  and a table }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 customers}{\insrsid7218531  in this data source.  The table }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 customers}{\insrsid7218531  must have columns }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 EmailAddress}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 FullName}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid536461 {\insrsid7218531 An example of using the Database Mail List Plugin is provided in the appendix on }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Database Examples}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 DatabasePluginExamples}{\insrsid7218531 .
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid8018829 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  Monitoring}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Monitoring}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Monitoring}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Monitoring
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Monitoring}}}{\insrsid7218531 There are two ways that you can monitor the operation of your }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  server.  You can monitor activity using the Performance Monitor, or log a range of information to one or more log files, to the Event Viewer, and to an ODBC database. 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  Logging}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Logging}}}{\insrsid7218531  Logging
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Logging}}}{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  supports three categories of logging: server logging, operation logging and error logging. 
\par {\pard\plain\f10\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'a7\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f10\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'a7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls54\pnrnot0\pnf10\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'a7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls54\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 Server logging is concerned with events such as services starting up and closing down, manual commands to retry domains, and configuration reloads.
\par {\pard\plain\f10\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'a7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f10\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'a7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls54\pnrnot0\pnf10\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'a7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls54\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 Operation logging is concerned with network connections made and released, protocol exchanges and transaction summaries.
\par {\pard\plain\f10\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'a7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f10\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af10\dbch\af0\hich\f10 \'a7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls54\pnrnot0\pnf10\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'a7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls54\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 Error logging is concerned with protocol syntax/sequence errors, failed protocol commands, authentication errors, and network or file I/O errors.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 You can record this log information in three different places:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-360\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 In log files. Each of the three logging categories has its own log file, created in a configurable log directory.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 In the Application Event Log.  Use the Event Viewer application, which you can find in the Administrative Tools program group, to examine the Event Log.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 In an ODBC database.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 To control logging, use the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Logs Folder}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 LogFolder}{\insrsid7218531  in the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Windows }{\uldb\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 WindowsConsoleReference}{\insrsid7218531 .  Refer to the }{\insrsid1670342 Eudora}{\insrsid7218531  web site for a comprehensive list of error codes.
