\par }\pard\plain \s90\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa120\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid8018829 \b\f1\fs40\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375 \page }{\cs98\cf0\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailSiteEngineChapter}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  WorldMail Engine}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  WorldMail Engine}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  }{\cs113\f4\insrsid536461\charrsid1928375 WorldMail}{\cs113\f4\insrsid7218531\charrsid1928375  Engine
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Engine}}}{\insrsid7218531 The }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Engine consists of seven services, which are equivalent to UNIX daemons such as }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 sendmail}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 pop3}{\insrsid7218531 . These services are:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 SMTPDA}{\insrsid7218531 , which handles outgoing SMTP transactions. This is the service responsible for routing messages to remote domains.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 SMTPRA}{\insrsid7218531 , which handles incoming SMTP transactions. This is the service that receives mail from other sites.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 POP3A}{\insrsid7218531 , which provides mail client access through the POP3 protocol.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 IMAP4A}{\insrsid7218531 , which provides mail client access through the IMAP4 protocol.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MAILMA}{\insrsid7218531 , which is used by the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  to remotely manage mailbox and mail list data, and allows Eudora users to change their e-mail password.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 HTTPMA}{\insrsid7218531 , which allows users to access to the Web }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  with a web browser.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls55\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls55\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 LDAP3A}{\insrsid7218531 , which provides access to account information through the LDAP protocol.
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 The following sections provide details about these services and other }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  resources.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  SMTPReceiverService}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  SMTP Receiver Service}}}{\insrsid7218531  SMTP Receiver Service
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  SMTPRA}}}{\insrsid7218531 The Receiver implements the SMTP Internet mail standard.  It appears to the outside world exactly the same as a UNIX }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 sendmail}{\insrsid7218531  server.
\par The Receiver listens for incoming messages on TCP/IP port 25. It places the messages in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 incoming}{\insrsid7218531  mail directory.
\par A message is stored as two separate files, named }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 uniquename.MSG}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 uniquename.RCP.}{\insrsid7218531   The }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 uniquename}{\insrsid7218531  is a unique identifier by which the message is known while it is in the system.
\par The }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSG}{\insrsid7218531  file contains the message itself.  The file is byte-stuffed (i.e. a redundant dot is inserted at the beginning of lines which start with a dot), and the end of the file is indicated by a single dot on a line by itself.
\par The }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 RCP}{\insrsid7218531  file contains the names of the recipients of the message, and the originator of the message (to whom non-delivery reports will be sent).
\par The Receiver will log incoming and outgoing transactions if the Logging options are set. This can be useful for analyzing mail transactions and errors.
\par The service is multi-threaded. This means that it can handle multiple connections from other mail servers at the same time.
\par The SMTP Receiver Service implements the SMTP and Extended SMTP protocols (ESMTP) defined in RFCs 821, 1652, 1869, 1870, 1985.  Refer to }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 http://www.rfc-editor.org}{\insrsid7218531  for a complete list of RFCs.
\par The following SMTP commands are supported:
\par }\pard\plain \s58\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\rtlgutter\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531       HELO       DATA \txne\line       EHLO       RSET \txne\line       QUIT       NOOP \txne\line       MAIL       VRFY\txne\line       RCPT
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The following Extended SMTP commands are supported:
\par }\pard\plain \s58\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\rtlgutter\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531       SIZE       8BITMIME
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 By default, a command of the form }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 VRFY name@domain.com}{\insrsid7218531  will return a successful response if the server accepts mail for domain.com. If }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Enable Full VRFY Support}{\insrsid7218531  is set using the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Security}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 SMTPSecurity}{\insrsid7218531  window, then this service will give information about whether }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 name@domain.com}{\insrsid7218531  is a mailbox or a mail list (or is unknown).
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  SMTPDeliveryService}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  SMTP Delivery Service}}}{\insrsid7218531  SMTP Delivery Service
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  SMTPDA}}}{\insrsid7218531 The SMTP Delivery Service is the internal sorter for }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 .  It deals with messages that have been received by the SMTP Receiver.
\par It moves messages from the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 incoming}{\insrsid7218531  directory, and stores them in a }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 holding}{\insrsid7218531  directory. For each distinct domain in the list of message recipients, the service creates a subdirectory (within the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 domains}{\insrsid7218531  directory), where it places information about the recipients in that directory.
\par For local deliveries, the service temporarily stores recipient information in a special }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 $local$}{\insrsid7218531  subdirectory within the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 domains}{\insrsid7218531  directory. It then copies messages into each local recipient's }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 inbox}{\insrsid7218531  directory.
\par For mail that is destined elsewhere, the service will submit a DNS request for a MX record for the corresponding domain. (It determines the DNS server address from the computer's TCP/IP configuration, so you must configure your computer with a correct DNS server address.)  It uses the MX record to determine the TCP/IP address(es) to which it should attempt to send messages for that domain. The service will attempt to establish contact with the mail server at that domain and transmit the message.  If unsuccessful, it will wait a while before attempting to contact the mail server again. It will persistently try to contact the mail server for several days, according to the Retry Schedule.
\par The message files in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 holding}{\insrsid7218531  directory are of the form }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 uniquename.MSG}{\insrsid7218531 . These files are byte-stuffed (i.e. a redundant dot is inserted at the beginning of lines which start with a dot), and the end of the file is indicated by a single dot on a line by itself.
\par The files in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 domains}{\insrsid7218531  directory are of the form }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 uniquename.RCP}{\insrsid7218531 . These files contain the names of the recipients of the message, and the originator of the message (to whom non-delivery reports will be sent).
\par The }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 domains}{\insrsid7218531  directory also contains a file }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 DOMAIN.MRI}{\insrsid7218531  that records routing information and details of how many times the SMTP Delivery Agent has attempted to contact each domain.
\par The SMTP Delivery Agent is multi-threaded and can deliver mail to multiple destinations at the same time.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  POP3Server}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  POP3 Server}}}{\insrsid7218531  POP3 Server
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  POP3A}}}{\insrsid7218531 The POP3 server implements the Post Office Protocol version 3 Internet standard.   It is responsible for passing incoming mail messages to e-mail clients.
\par It listens on TCP/IP port 110 for connections from e-mail clients. When a mail client connects, the server authenticates the username and password. If the username and password are valid then the server transfers messages from a user's }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 inbox}{\insrsid7218531  directory to the mail client program.
\par The server logs transactions if the Logging options are set.  The service is multi-threaded. This means that multiple clients can pickup their mail at the same time.
\par The POP3 Service implements RFCs 1734, 1939, and 2095.    Refer to }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 http://www.rfc-editor.org}{\insrsid7218531  for a complete list of RFCs.
\par The following POP3 commands are supported:
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\rtlgutter\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531       USER name \txne\line       PASS string\txne\line       APOP string\txne\line       AUTH \txne\line       STAT \txne\line       LIST [msg] \txne\line       RETR msg \txne\line       DELE msg \txne\line       NOOP \txne\line       RSET \txne\line       TOP msg n \txne\line       UIDL [msg]\txne\line       QUIT
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  IMAP4Server}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  IMAP4 Server}}}{\insrsid7218531  IMAP4 Server
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  IMAP4A}}}{\insrsid7218531 The IMAP4 server implements the Internet Mail Access Protocol version 4 standard.  The IMAP4 protocol provides a rich interface for managing mail in a mailbox on a remote server.
\par The IMAP4 server provides an alternate way for mail users to logon and read their e-mail.  It provides all of the capabilities of the POP3 service, with some major enhancements.
\par The IMAP4 protocol makes it possible for mail users to leave their messages on the server and organize them into folders.
\par This is very useful for people that use more than one computer to read their mail.  Using the IMAP protocol, they can walk up to any computer that has an IMAP client installed, can log onto their mailbox and read their e-mail.
\par The IMAP4 Service implements RFCs 2060, 2086, 2095.    Refer to }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 http://www.rfc-editor.org}{\insrsid7218531  for a complete list of RFCs.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  LDAP3AServer}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  LDAP3 Server}}}{\insrsid7218531  LDAP3 Server
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  LDAP3A}}}{\insrsid7218531 The LDAP3 server implements the Lightweight Directory Access Protocol version 3 standard.  The LDAP3 protocol allows e-mail clients to search for names and addresses of users on the server.
\par Users search the LDAP3 server by creating a new directory service account in their e-mail client and submitting a query from the address book.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  HTTPManagementServer}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  HTTP Management Server}}}{\insrsid7218531  HTTP Management Server
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  HTTPMA}}}{\insrsid7218531 The HTTP server provides a way for }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  users to configure their mailbox properties through any Web browser.
\par When a user connects with a Web browser, a Login form is displayed.  If the user enters a valid username and password then the Mailbox Properties form will be displayed.  This form allows the user to change his mailbox properties, such as the AutoReply and Reply Message.  This is useful if the user is going on vacation and wants }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to automatically reply to all of his incoming mail with a vacation message.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MAILMAServer}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  MAILMA Server}}}{\insrsid7218531  MAILMA Server
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  MAILMA}}}{\insrsid7218531 The function of the Mail Management Agent is to listen on port 106 and allow Eudora mail clients to change mailbox passwords.  It also communicates with the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  to allow }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  administration to be performed remotely over a TCP/IP connection.
\par The Change Password protocol is very simple, and is best documented by example.  Here }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 S}{\insrsid7218531  is the server, }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 C}{\insrsid7218531  is the client:
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \brdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp80 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\rtlgutter\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 S: 200 HELLO\txne\line C: USER yourloginname\txne\line S: 300 Please send your password now\txne\line C: PASS yourcurrentpassword\txne\line S: 200 Ok\txne\line C: NEWPASS yournewpassword\txne\line S: 200 Ok\txne\line C: QUIT\txne\line S: 200 Bye-bye\\r\\n\txne\line S: <closes connection>\txne\line C: <closes connection>}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  WorkingDirectories}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Working Directories}}}{\insrsid7218531  Working Directories
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 This section describes how }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  uses directories to spool mail.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailboxDirectory}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailbox Directory}}}{\insrsid7218531  Mailbox Directory }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mailbox directories}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,Mailboxes}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Each }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  user has a separate mailbox directory.  The }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Mailbox Directory}{\insrsid7218531  in the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Domain General Page}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 DomainGeneralPage}{\insrsid7218531  in the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  sets the mailbox directory location. The SMTP Delivery Agent delivers mail into this directory.  The POP3 and IMAP4 services may remove mail from this directory under control of a e-mail client.
{\v0\par\v}It is highly recommended that you store your mailboxes on an NTFS partition.  During installation, the Windows user that the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  services run as is granted Full Control the default mailbox root directory.  If you move this directory after installation, or if you create additional mailbox root directories for virtual domains, you must manually grant the }{\insrsid536461 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  user Full Control over these directories (and all subdirectories).
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  MailSpoolDirectory}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail Spool Directory}}}{\insrsid7218531  Mail Spool Directory }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Mail Spool directory}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,Spool}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 You can use the }{\insrsid14683656 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531  to specify the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Mail Spool Directory}{\insrsid7218531 . The spool directory contains a number of subdirectories that are used as }{\i\insrsid7218531 staging posts}{\insrsid7218531  for messages.  On Windows NT it is recommended that the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Mail Spool Directory}{\insrsid7218531  is on an NTFS partition.  The directory structure under the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Mail Spool Directory}{\insrsid7218531  is as follows.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 incoming }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,incoming}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 This directory holds messages received by the SMTP Receiver. The SMTP Delivery Agent also places messages here, for example, non-delivery reports and messages which are sent to mail lists.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 holding }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,holding}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The SMTP Delivery Agent moves messages from the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 incoming}{\insrsid7218531  directory into this directory.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 domains }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,domains}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 When a message is moved into the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 holding}{\insrsid7218531  directory, the SMTP Delivery Agent creates a subdirectory within the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 domains}{\insrsid7218531  directory for each separate domain to which the message is addressed.  If the message is addressed to a local user, it creates a subdirectory called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 $local$}{\insrsid7218531 . In each subdirectory it stores routing information and information about the message recipients in that domain. (The message itself stays in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 holding}{\insrsid7218531  directory.) 
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 dead }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,dead}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 This directory collects messages which are both undeliverable and un-returnable.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 lists }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,lists}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 This directory contains subdirectories corresponding to mail lists. For every mail list, two directories are created: one corresponding to the list itself, and one corresponding to the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 -request}{\insrsid7218531  address for the list.  Messages are moved into these directories temporarily while they are being delivered to list members.
