\par You can also specify a single wildcard as the first character of the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Map To}{\insrsid7218531  field. This will be replaced by the actual user name when the table entry is used. For instance, if the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Map From}{\insrsid7218531  string is }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 f*}{\insrsid7218531  and the corresponding }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Map To}{\insrsid7218531  string is }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 *-blue@xyz.com}{\insrsid7218531 , then a message for }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 fred@abc.com}{\insrsid7218531  will be redirected to }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 fred-blue@xyz.com}{\insrsid7218531 .
