\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Agents}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Server Agent}}}{\insrsid7218531 Click the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Agents}{\insrsid7218531  icon to configure the Server Agent and the Archive Directory:
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1024\langfe1024\cgrid\noproof\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid13778604 \{bmc windows console - agents - 256c.bmp\}}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid13778604  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid13778604 
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Incoming Mail Agent
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  executes the Server Agent for every message that is received.  The agent is passed the names of two files: the message file itself, and a file containing SMTP envelope information.
\par The }{\i\insrsid7218531 message file}{\insrsid7218531  is a text file with a }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSG}{\insrsid7218531  extension.  The file containing the SMTP envelope information is known as the }{\i\insrsid7218531 recipients file}{\insrsid7218531 , although it contains more than just recipient information. The recipients file is a text file with a }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 RCO}{\insrsid7218531  extension when it is passed to the Server Agent.  When the agent terminates, }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will rename the file to its normal }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 RCP}{\insrsid7218531  extension.
\par This field should contain a command-line template.  An occurrence of }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 %r}{\insrsid7218531  in the template is replaced by the name of the recipients file, and an occurrence of }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 %m}{\insrsid7218531  in the template is replaced by the name of the message file.  The resulting command line is then passed to the command-line interpreter to execute.
\par Thus, if the template were:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls58\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls58\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 copy "%r" c:\\temp & copy "%m" c:\\temp
\par }\pard \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 {\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  would copy both the message file and the recipients file to the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 c:\\temp}{\insrsid7218531  directory.
\par Multiple commands can be executed, as in the above example, by separating each command with the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 &}{\insrsid7218531  character (or by using a batch file).
\par The agent is executed by the SMTPRA service and agent inherits the access rights of the SMTPRA service.  If you installed }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to run its services as a specific Windows user, you must grant this user execute access for the agent application.
\par It is important that the Server Agent should not take too long to execute.  Otherwise, a busy mail server could easily run out of memory or saturate its processor.
\par It is possible for the Server Agent to delete or move the message file and recipients files - for instance if the agent determines that the message contains a virus.  In this case, the agent should respect the wishes of the sender regarding delivery status notifications, as expressed in the recipients file.  This means that the agent may need to send a Delivery Status Notification message. Not to do so may be a violation of the SMTP protocol.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Archive Directory
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Directories,Archive}}}{\insrsid7218531  }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Archive Agent}}}{\insrsid7218531 A copy of every incoming message can be archived to a directory by entering the directory name in this field.  }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will create a folder under this directory with the name equal to the current date.  }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will copy every incoming }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSG}{\insrsid7218531  message file and corresponding }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 RCP}{\insrsid7218531  recipients file into this directory.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid8018829 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  ConfigurationConnector}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Configuration Connector}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Configuration Connector}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  Configuration Connector
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The Configuration Connector controls the method that }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  uses to store its c}{\insrsid8018829 onfiguration and mailbox data. WorldMail is installed using the Registry Connector, which stores all configuration data in the Windows registry.  }{\insrsid7218531 Your license }{\insrsid8018829 does}{\insrsid7218531  not allow you to configure this option.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid8018829 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  BannerInsertion}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Banner Insertion}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Banner Insertion}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  Banner Insertion
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Click the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Banner Insertion}{\insrsid7218531  icon to configure the e-mail banners to be added to all messages received via SMTP:
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1024\langfe1024\cgrid\noproof\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid13778604 \{bmc windows console - banners - 256c.bmp\}}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid13778604  }{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531\charrsid13778604 
\par }{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 Banners can be defined at the domain level and the server level. Domain-level banners are added to all messages sent that domain, while server banners are added to all mail sent from remote domains (that is, domains not defined in }{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 ).
\par There are two types of banners: }{\b\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 Header}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 Footer}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 . Headers are inserted at the top of the body of the email message, while footers are appended to the bottom of the message body (above all attachments).
\par You can set separate banners for plain text messages and HTML messages. This allows you to insert sophisticated HTML content (including banner advertisement graphics) in messages that contain HTML. If an HTML banner is not defined, the plain text banners for the domain are applied to both text and HTML messages.}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid3758023 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  SecurityFolder}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Security}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Security}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  Security
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  provides security features to help protect your server against abuse and unsolicited commercial e-mail (also known as }{\i\insrsid7218531 spam }{\cs98\i\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Spam}}}{\insrsid7218531 ).  }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  Security features can be seen by double-clicking on the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Security }{\insrsid7218531 icon:
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid12648643 \{bmc windows console - security - 256c.bmp\}}{\insrsid12648643  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid12648643 
\par }{\insrsid7218531 These Security properties help you block unauthorized use of your mail server.  It is easy to block authorized access to your mail server by mistake, so take great care to set these properties.  Refer to the section on }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Advanced SMTP Security}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 AdvancedSMTPSecurity}{\insrsid7218531  for more information. You can also set these policies through the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Anti-Relay Wizard}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 AntiRelayWizard}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Anti-Spam Wizard}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 AntiSpamWizard}{\insrsid7218531 .}{\b\i\insrsid7218531 
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid3758023 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  GeneralPropertyPage}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  General Security Settings}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  General Security Settings}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  General Security Settings
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  SMTP Security}}}{\insrsid7218531 The Security Properties dialog is invoked by double-clicking on the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Security Properties}{\insrsid7218531  icon:
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid13778604 \{bmc security properties - general 256c.bmp\}}{\insrsid13778604  }{\insrsid7218531\charrsid13778604 
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Enable Full VRFY Support
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 VRFY }{\cs98\b\f2\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  VRFY}}}{\insrsid7218531  is an SMTP command that allows sending mail servers to verify the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 To}{\insrsid7218531 : address.  By default, a command of the form }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 VRFY name@domain.com}{\insrsid7218531  will return a successful response if this server accepts mail for }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 domain.com}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par If }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Enable Full VRFY Support}{\insrsid7218531  is set, then }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will respond to the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 VRFY}{\insrsid7218531  command with information about whether }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 name@domain.com}{\insrsid7218531  is known, and if so whether it is a mailbox or a mail list. 
\par If you leave this box unchecked, it reduces the amount of information an attacker or spammer can find out about your users.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Authenticated ETRN }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  ETRN}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The SMTP }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 ETRN}{\insrsid7218531  command is used to request an SMTP server to start sending mail for a particular domain.  (This command is used by the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MSSTART}{\insrsid7218531  utility.)  If you check this box then the SMTP client must be authenticated (using the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 AUTH}{\insrsid7218531  command with a valid mailbox name and password), otherwise the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 ETRN}{\insrsid7218531  command will be rejected.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Maximum message size (bytes)
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Enter the maximum message size in bytes that the SMTP Receiver will accept. The default is 0, which means that there is no size limit apart from memory and disc space constraints.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Header Rewrite Mode }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Header rewriting}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Select a format that }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will use to rewrite an invalid }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 From}{\insrsid7218531  header address.  The choices are:
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li115\tx115 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls89\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls89\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 None
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls89\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls89\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 "Jane User" <user@domain>
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\fi-720\li1080\tx1080 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\tx1080\li1080\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls89\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'de}}\tx1080 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls89\adjustright\rin130\txn1080\lin1080\itap0 {\insrsid7218531 user@domain (Jane User)
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Use Alternate Resent Headers }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Resent headers}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 This option controls the way that }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  defines }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Resent}{\insrsid7218531  headers, which are used to save information about forwarded messages.  By default, resent headers are created in the format }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Resent-Header}{\insrsid7218531 , such as }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Resent-To}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Resent-From}{\insrsid7218531 .  You can change the format of resent headers by enabling this field, which causes these headers to be created in the format }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 X-Resent-Header}{\insrsid7218531 .
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 Anti-Denial-of-Service: Max connections (all hosts)
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 This setting provides a limit to the total number of incoming SMTP connections that }{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531  will respond to at any time. When this number of connections are active, SMTPRA will no longer accept new connections until a current connection has been closed.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 Anti-Denial-of-Service: Max connections per host
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 This setting limits the number of incoming SMTP connections allowed from any one system. When this number of SMTP connections from any one host are active, SMTPRA will no longer accept new connections from that host. This option is very useful for containing potential damage from an abusive system without blocking incoming connections from other (non-abusive) systems.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 Anti-Denial-of-Service: Connection timeout
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 This option sets a limit to the number of seconds that }{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531  will keep open a non-responsive SMTP connection.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 Anti-Denial-of-Service: Limit throughput from each host
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531 This option provides a throttle on the amount of data (in kilobytes per second) that SMTPRA will accept from any one host. This allows you to control DoS attacks that send large amounts of data over relatively few connections. When using this option it is recommended that you exempt your "friendly" hosts from this limit to avoid slowing mail traffic from your own network.}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid3758023 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  AntiSpamPropertyPage}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  Anti-Spam Security Properties}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Anti-Spam Security Properties}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  Anti-Spam Security Properties
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The Anti-Spam Security Properties dialog is invoked by clicking on the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Anti Spam }{\insrsid7218531 tab:
\par }{\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1024\langfe1024\cgrid\noproof\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid7362620 \{bmc security properties - anti-spam 256c.bmp\}}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7362620  }{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531\charrsid7362620 
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Lookup SMTP hosts in the DNS
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  DNS}}}{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can be configured to perform a reverse lookup of the IP address of the incoming SMTP host.  The resulting host name is used in the log files and in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Received:}{\insrsid7218531  header.  If the reverse lookup fails then connection is rejected unless the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Accept Unknown Hosts}{\insrsid7218531  option is turned on.
\par This option can help block unauthorized SMTP relay because many junk mail distributors do not have a valid reverse DNS record.
\par This option can have a serious impact on performance.  }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  must submit a reverse DNS lookup query for each incoming connection.  If your DNS server is slow then incoming connections may experience significant delays.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Lookup SMTP hosts using blacklist server(s)
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 This option allows }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  to block messages coming from known sources of junk email, as compiled by blacklist servers. If you check this box, and a host listed with the given blacklist server connects to }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 , then all mail from that server will be rejected. Note that checking this box may slow down the rate at which you can accept mail because of the extra time required to perform the lookup.
\par To use this option, specify the host name of the blacklist server in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Blacklist servers}{\insrsid7218531  field. When entering multiple values in field separate each entry with a comma.
\par When using blacklist servers it is recommended that you exempt your "friendly" hosts from blacklist lookup. This will prevent numerous unnecessary blacklist queries that would otherwise slow }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531 's SMTP performance.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Require SMTP authentication for relaying }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Authenticated SMTP}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Checking this option requires that anyone relaying mail through your SMTP server must log in via Authenticated SMTP. This prevents unknown users from using your server to relay junk mail. However, this also requires that all of your end users have mail clients that support Authenticated SMTP and that they enable this feature in their client.
\par This feature also includes and option to exempt your "friendly" hosts from SMTP authentication.  Enabling this option allows non-authenticated SMTP traffic from hosts listed under the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Accept mail for relay from these friendly hosts\'85}{\insrsid7218531  option. 
\par When this option is selected, the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Disable authenticated SMTP}{\insrsid7218531  option in this window is automatically disabled. 
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Disable relay for non-local users
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Checking this box is a quick way to stop your mail server being used to relay spam to other sites.  If you check this, then }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will not accept mail for relay unless the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MAIL FROM:}{\insrsid7218531  address in the SMTP envelope refers to a local domain.  (Note that the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MAIL FROM:}{\insrsid7218531  address specifies the return address for non-delivery reports - it is not necessarily the same as the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 From:}{\insrsid7218531  address in the message header.)
\par This option will not protect your mail server against determined spammers, who are capable of forging the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MAIL FROM:}{\insrsid7218531  address.  You can get better protection using the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Require SMTP authentication for relaying}{\insrsid7218531  option, or through the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Accept mail for relay from these friendly hosts}{\insrsid7218531  mask list.  (Note that if you set up the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Accept mail for relay from these friendly hosts}{\insrsid7218531  list, you should turn off this option since it overrides the value in that field.)
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Validate sender address
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 If you check this box }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will look up the domain name supplied in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MAIL FROM:}{\insrsid7218531  command, to ensure that there is a valid A record or MX record in the DNS for it.  If there is not, the address is assumed to be illegal, and the mail will be rejected.  Turning this on may reduce performance since the DNS server may take some time to respond.}{\b\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Max number of recipients per message
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 You can specify the maximum number of recipients allowed for an individual message. These are the recipients specified on the SMTP envelope (that is, given by the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 RCPT TO:}{\insrsid7218531  command).  If you specify 0, there is no maximum.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Disable authenticated SMTP }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Authenticated SMTP}}}{\insrsid7218531 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Check this option if you do not want to use authenticated SMTP to control mail relay. Enabling this field automatically disables the }{\b\insrsid7218531 Require SMTP authentication for relaying}{\insrsid7218531  field.
