\par }{\insrsid7218531 A Domain Synonym is a name that is equivalent to the virtual domain in question.  If your virtual domain is }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 xyz.com}{\insrsid7218531 , and you create a synonym of }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 xyzcompany.com}{\insrsid7218531 , then mail addressed to }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 you@xyzcompany.com}{\insrsid7218531  will go to }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 you@xyz.com}{\insrsid7218531 .  See the section on }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Multiple Domains}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 Domains}{\insrsid7218531  for further information on synonyms.
