\par }{\insrsid7218531 Mail servers that act as intermediaries in mail delivery are often referred to as "}{\b\insrsid7218531 relays}{\insrsid7218531 ." When your system is acting as a relay, messages meant for other computers will be placed in your server's queue and delivered accordingly. }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  can act as an Internet gateway relaying mail to and from the Internet. Internet gateways have no local users. A }{\b\insrsid7218531 relay host}{\insrsid7218531  handles local users. 
\par The checkbox on this dialog enables or disables domain forwarding for this domain. 
\par All mail addressed to this domain will be automatically forwarded to the hostname specified on this page. Any valid domain name or IP address may also be entered in this field. 
\par The "Reattempt delivery to this host now!" button will force an instant attempt to deliver any queued mail for this domain to the specified host. This button will only work when forwarding is enabled and will be disabled until the button is pressed again.
