\par }{\insrsid7218531 This form contains a list of NT Users that can be used to create mailboxes. Previously defined users will not appear.
\par Users identified by the computer icon are Local Users.  This means that the account has been created in the User Manager on your }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  server.
\par Users identified by the server icon are Domain Users.  This means that the account has been created on the Domain Controller to which your }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  server belongs.
\par Select one or more Windows NT user that you wish to enable for sending and receiving mail.  Use the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Shift}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Control}{\insrsid7218531  keys to select multiple users.
\par Note that it is not a good idea to select NT user names containing spaces or underlines.  Although }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  will handle such names correctly, many mail clients and other mail software will have problems.  Enclosing the name in double quotes when sending mail to it, such as }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 "Fred Jones"@abc.com}{\insrsid7218531 , may help, but such names are better avoided altogether.
\par You can create mailboxes for members of a NT Group by clicking on the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Add NT Group}{\insrsid7218531  button.  You can automatically create NT mailboxes.  See the section on the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 NT Mailbox Plugin}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 NTMailboxPluginConfiguration}{\insrsid7218531  for more information.
