\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls141\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls141\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Goodbye Message}{\insrsid7218531 , which is sent when someone }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 LEAVE}{\insrsid7218531 s or }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 UNSUBSCRIBE}{\insrsid7218531 s to the list.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls141\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls141\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Message Prolog}{\insrsid7218531 , which is inserted at the beginning of each list message.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls141\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls141\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Message Postscript}{\insrsid7218531 , which is appended to the end of each list message.
\par {\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\fi-360\li720\tx720 \tab}{\*\pntextbsx\pard\plain\f3\fs16\insrsid7218531 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\tx720\li720\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\jclisttab{\*\pnbsx \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls141\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'b7}}\tx720 \aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls141\adjustright\rin130\txn720\lin720\itap0\pararsid15231392 {\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Help Message}{\insrsid7218531 , which is sent in response to the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 HELP}{\insrsid7218531  command.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 List Message Text
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Enter the text that you would like the list command processor to return to the sender.  Use message directives for advanced message processing.
\par If you want to put a large amount of text into your message, use the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 %INCLUDE}{\insrsid7218531  directive, rather than typing text into the configuration console directly. This is to save space in the Registry. In fact, you will find that the configuration console will only accept a relatively small amount of text\'3b enough for a short message and a few directives.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \b\f2\fs16\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 Message Prologs and Postscripts
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 You can arrange for each message sent to the list to have a prolog or postscript added. This is very useful for reminding list members how to leave the list. Use the corresponding dropdown items in the Messages page in the list properties form to set this up.
\par You may use the same message directives as for Welcome and Goodbye messages, but the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 %ADDRESS}{\insrsid7218531  directive will be replaced by the address of the mailing list, not the address of an individual recipient. Other remarks in the preceding section also apply to prologs and postscripts.
\par If a message to a mail list contains a MIME }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Content-type:}{\insrsid7218531  header, and the content type is not text/plain, neither the prolog nor the postscript will be added. This is to avoid corrupting data such as image, movie, etc.
