\par }{\insrsid7218531 You can use this page to edit the properties of your mail list.  It contains a number of tabbed pages that operate in a similar manner to the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Mail List Property}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ListGeneralPage}{\insrsid7218531  pages in the Windows }{\insrsid8736596 Management Center}{\insrsid7218531 .   Refer to the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 Windows }{\uldb\insrsid8736596 Management Center}{\uldb\insrsid7218531  Reference}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 WindowsConsoleReference}{\insrsid7218531  section for more information.
{\v0\par\v}}{\lang2057\langfe1033\langnp2057\insrsid7218531 The mail list General tab contains a Moderate button that takes you into the }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe1033\langnp2057\insrsid7218531 Pending Page}{\v\uldb\lang2057\langfe1033\langnp2057\insrsid7218531 WebPendingPage}{\lang2057\langfe1033\langnp2057\insrsid7218531 .  Here you can moderate pending messages for the mail list.
{\v0\par\v}}\pard\plain \s2\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb120\sa40\keepn\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0\pararsid8130183 \b\f1\fs28\cf17\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 \page }{\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 #}{\insrsid15606814  WebListModeration}}${\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 $}{\insrsid15606814  List Moderation}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  List Moderation}}+{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 +}{\insrsid15606814  mailsite:0000}}}{\insrsid7218531  List Moderation
\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid7218531 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s97\ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs98\super\insrsid15606814 K}{\insrsid15606814  Web Management Center,List Moderation}}}{\insrsid7218531 Content Moderation is a feature that allows mail list moderators to approve or reject all messages sent to a mail list.  To enable this feature, select the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Moderator controls content}{\insrsid7218531  feature in the }{\uldb\insrsid7218531 List General Page}{\v\uldb\insrsid7218531 ListGeneralPage}{\insrsid7218531 .
{\v0\par\v}When a new message arrives at the server, it will be checked to see if its author may post to the list.  If the author does not have posting permission (for instance, if he is not a member of the mail list and the mail list is set to disallow posting by non-members), the message will be returned to the author with an appropriate rejection message.  If the author does have permission, delivery processing depends on whether content moderation is enabled for the list.
{\v0\par\v}If content moderation is enabled, then the message will be placed in the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 pending}{\insrsid7218531  directory for that list.  If content moderation is not enabled, then the message is placed directly into the mail list directory.
{\v0\par\v}For example, suppose there is a mail list called }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 discuss}{\insrsid7218531  in the default domain and this list has content moderation enabled.  If the mail list directory is called:
