\par }\pard\plain \ql \tx115\li115\ri130\sb80\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin130\txn115\lin115\itap0 \f1\fs16\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid7218531 The next step is to configure }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  so that it logs information to your new database.  Read the chapter that discusses logging carefully, and in the Database Log Configuration dialog, fill in the data source name, the user ID and password if required.
\par Unless you have adopted the default database table structure outlined above, you will also need to modify the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 VALUES}{\insrsid7218531  clause in the SQL template.
\par You should replace }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 MailLog}{\insrsid7218531  in the default template with the name of your table.  You should also replace the column names in the default template with your own column names.
\par If you have decided to use fewer than fourteen columns in your table, you will need to modify the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 VALUES}{\insrsid7218531  clause in the SQL template.  When adding a row to the table, }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  replaces every occurrence of }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 %1}{\insrsid7218531  in the SQL template with the name of the server, }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 %2}{\insrsid7218531  with the category value, and so on through }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 %13}{\insrsid7218531 .  (See above for a complete list of the substitution parameters.)  The default SQL template records all thirteen parameters\'3b however, you can omit parameters from the SQL template if you do not wish to log the corresponding information.
\par Note that the first column in the default SQL template (}{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Tlog}{\insrsid7218531 ) gets its value from the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 getdate()}{\insrsid7218531  built-in SQL function.  It has no corresponding substitution parameter.
\par If your table uses widths for the text columns (the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Service}{\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 Px}{\insrsid7218531  columns or their equivalents in your table) which differ from the default widths, you will need to tell }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  about the new widths.  Click the Advanced button, and enter the new widths into the resulting Advanced dialog.  This ensures that }{\insrsid13722995 WorldMail}{\insrsid7218531  truncates the text values if necessary (because storing a long string in a column too small for it causes a SQL error).
\par Finally, select the options you wish to log to the database in each of the Server, operation and Error categories.  Dismiss the configuration console.  The services will now start logging information to the database.
\par If you have problems with database logging, turn on file logging of General Errors.  The error log file should indicate the nature of the problem.
