\par A typical exchange is shown below.  Lines starting }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 C:}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531  are sent by the client\'3b lines starting }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 S:}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531  are sent by the server.  (Of course, the }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 C:}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531  and }{\b\f2\insrsid7218531 S:}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid7218531  are not actually part of the protocol!)
